<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#description -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#description">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«JSON::JSON_Attribute»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>description</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Description of the trouble or issue</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#name -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#name">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«JSON::JSON_Attribute»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>name</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Name of the trouble ticket, typically a short description provided by the user that create the ticket</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableCode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableCode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>(un)applicableCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicator that specifies whether an instance represents applicability or un-applicability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableDays -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableDays">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>(un)applicableDays</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A day or days representing applicability or un-applicability.  For example 2, 3 represent Monday and Tuesday.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableDuring -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#(un)applicableDuring">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>(un)applicableDuring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A period of time representing applicability or un-applicability. For example, from 8AM to 12PM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EmployeePay</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>amount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount corresponds to the sum of each EmployeePayComponent amount (calculated if it's a rate) for the EmployeePay period.  It specifies the unit (any currency) and the value such as $10.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amoutPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amoutPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EmployeePay</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>amoutPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>amountPeriod specifies the duration covered by the amount. For example, the amount may correspond to a complete Year.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#abbreviation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#abbreviation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TimeZoneRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>abbreviation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptableEquipmentList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptableEquipmentList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>acceptableEquipmentList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of strings, based on M.3100, that identifies the types of equipment objects that can be supported by this object. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptableEquipmentTypeList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptableEquipmentTypeList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>acceptableEquipmentTypeList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the types of equipment that can be supported by the Equipment Holder.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptedAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acceptedAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DAAAccepted</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>acceptedAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount which the enterprise agreed to refund the Customer as a result of this DisputedAmount. This amount is less or equal the disputedAmount (in DAACreated entity), pending of the DisputedAmount was partially or completely accepted respectively.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessClassification -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessClassification">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>accessClassification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The access intended for this entry Permitted Values: PUBLIC, PRIVATE or CONFIDENTIAL</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessDecision -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessDecision">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NACSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>accessDecision</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Final decision by the NAC to permit or deny access to the network (Permit/Deny).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accessLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpact</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>accessLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Level of access obtained by the intruder, such as Root or User access.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accountNameInThirdParty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accountNameInThirdParty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ThirdPartyCollectionPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>accountNameInThirdParty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The account, which is used in the third party, used to pay. If bank transfer is used here,  paymentAccountinThirdParty is BankAccount. If paymet tool (such as PayPal) is used here, paymentAccountInThirdPart is the payment tool (such as PayPal) account.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accuracy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#accuracy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasure</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>accuracy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The number of digits of accuracy captured for Metrics associated with a MetricDefMeasure.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acFrequencyHigh -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acFrequencyHigh">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>acFrequencyHigh</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the high value of the AC Frequency range in Hertz. If this is a DC PowerSupply, this value is not applicable and should be set to NULL.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acFrequencyLow -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#acFrequencyLow">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>acFrequencyLow</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the low value of the AC Frequency range in Hertz. If this is a DC PowerSupply, this value is not applicable and should be set to NULL.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#achievedBudget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#achievedBudget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Budget</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>achievedBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount achieved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ackState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the Acknowledgement State of the alarm.   Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for acknowledgement state change.    If the acknowledgeResourceAlarms is supported, then this attribute shall also be supported.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ackStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acknowledgement status</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackSystemId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackSystemId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ackSystemId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the name of the system that last changed the ackState of an alarm, i.e. acknowledged or unacknowledged the alarm.  Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for acknowledgement state change.    If the acknowledgeResourceAlarms is supported, then this attribute is optional.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ackTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the time when the alarm has been last acknowledged or unacknowledged.  Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for acknowledgement state change.    If the acknowledgeResourceAlarms is supported, then this attribute shall also be supported.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackUserId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ackUserId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ackUserId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the id of the user who has last changed the ack state of the alarm,  i.e. acknowledged or unacknowledged the alarm.  Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for acknowledgement state change.    If the acknowledgeResourceAlarms is supported, then this attribute shall also be supported.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#action -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#action">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>action</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The action to take for an InteractionItem, such as add, change, remove.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionData -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionData">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionData</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute provides a general extension mechanism for representing policy actions that have not been modeled with the specific properties contained in this model. The format of this attribute is determined by the OID value stored in the ActionEncoding attribute. A policy decision point can readily determine whether it supports the values stored in an instance of ActionData by checking the OID value from ActionEncoding against the set of OIDs it recognizes. The action for the policy decision point to take in case it does not recognize the format of this data could itself be modeled as a PolicyRule, governing the behavior of the policy decision point. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called ActionData.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionEncoding -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionEncoding">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionEncoding</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute. It is used to represent an OID that in turn identifies the encoding and semantics of the ActionData attribute value array in this instance. The value of this property is a single string, representing a single OID. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called ActionEncoding.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionExecutionStrategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionExecutionStrategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionExecutionStrategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the execution strategy to be used upon the sequenced actions aggregated by this PolicyActionComposite object. Defined execution strategies include: 0: Unknown 1: Do Until Success 2: Do All 3: Do Until Failure 4: Do All Without Failure or Do Nothing "Do Until Success" means that actions should be executed according to their predefined order, until successful execution of a single action. At that point, the process should stop (even if there are additional actions that could be executed). "Do All" means that all actions should be executed that are part of the set, according to their predefined order. This should continue, even if one or more of the actions fails. "Do Until Failure" means that actions should be executed according to their predefined order until an action fails to execute. At that point, the entire sequence should be stopped. Finally, "Do All Without Failure or Do Nothing" means that ALL actions specified should be performed. However, if a failure occurs, then NONE of the actions should be performed. This implies EITHER the ability to look-ahead and ensure that the actions will be able to be performed successfully, or the ability to perform a rollback of that action and all previous actions when an error is encountered.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionItem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionItem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarToDo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionItem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionRequested -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionRequested">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemShipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionRequested</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Realize or Cancel</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionResponse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionResponse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionResponse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that is used to allow a 'standard' definition of a TRUE/FALSE response to be made by an external system attached to the model at this point. This will allow integration with a generalized policy processing engine. notes: Not defined in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionsCNF -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionsCNF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionsCNF</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a non-negative integer and represents the particular sequence in which this element is executed as part of the overall policy structure.   For example if a composite is part of another composite policy structure. Notes: default is “1”</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionSequenceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionSequenceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionSequenceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a non-negative integer and represents the particular sequence in which this element is executed as part of the overall policy structure. This will allow a policy engine to reference externally supplied arguments to this object as it is executed.  Notes: Not present in the ITU specs;  CIM 2.7 has a subset of these values.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionTaken -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actionTaken">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevShareReconDiscrepancy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actionTaken</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that describes what action was taken, such as the creation of a PartyRevenueShareAdjustment, an AppliedPartyBillingRate, an adjustment to a PartyPayment, or a PartyPaymentItem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activationMode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activationMode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>activationMode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether the designed service is activated through provisioning, or is signaled.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DisputedAmountActivity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>activityDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date in which this activity was performed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Activity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>activityNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique identifier for the Activity</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#activityStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>activityStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Activity status, indicates if the problem is historical or active</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualCompletionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualCompletionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarToDo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actualCompletionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date the toDo was actually completed Notes: COMPLETED [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforceResourceAssignment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actualCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Actual Cost of the assignment of the resource (tools) to the work.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actualDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The duration that actually occurred</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualParticipationStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#actualParticipationStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryAttendance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>actualParticipationStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ACWP -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ACWP">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ACWP</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Actual Cost of Work Scheduled</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalInfo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalInfo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToBeDeprecated»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>additionalInfo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a vendor specific attribute that contains additional specific information about the object. This list can be empty.  The attribute, when present, can be used to convey information from the target OS to the requesting OS, and vice versa, of additional information that isn't explicitly modelled, except that some parameter names and values may be predefined.  Any information encoded in the additionalInfo is optional: target OS need not fill out this information and the requesting OS need not interpret this information.  See R_TMF518_FMW_I_0001.This is a vendor specific attribute that contains additional specific information about the object. This list can be empty.  The attribute, when present, can be used to convey information from the target OS to the requesting OS, and vice versa, of additional information that isn't explicitly modelled, except that some parameter names and values may be predefined.  Any information encoded in the additionalInfo is optional: the target OS need not fill out this information and the requesting OS need not interpret this information.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalObjectInfoList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalObjectInfoList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TransmissionDescriptor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>additionalObjectInfoList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains additional parameters which can be set and/or retrieved on an object having this Transmission Descriptor (TMD) assigned as (egress or ingress) TMD.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalText -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#additionalText">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>additionalText</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains further information on the alarm. Vendors should avoid using this field to put additional information identifying the alarmed object or the specific problem. The corresponding fields should be use for better alarm quality.   This attribute is optional in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#addressValueList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#addressValueList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddressValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>addressValueList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of string values. Each string value contains a particular value to filter on. Note that all values must have the format specified in the Format attribute of this class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#adjustmentReason -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#adjustmentReason">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevenueShareAdjustment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>adjustmentReason</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The reason the adjustment was determined.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#administrativeState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#administrativeState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedHardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>administrativeState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that describes the current physical state of the ManagedHardware. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Unlocked  2: Locked  3: Shutting Down  4: Starting Up  5: Testing  6: Maintenance  7: Not Applicable  8: Not able to inform  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#adminState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#adminState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Test</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>adminState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The administrative state of the test may be "LOCKED", "UNLOCKED"</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#affectedServiceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#affectedServiceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceProblem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>affectedServiceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Number of affected services (mandatory, but value can be zero).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#afterSalesServiceProvidedBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#afterSalesServiceProvidedBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>afterSalesServiceProvidedBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that a party provides assurance related customer service after a sale is made.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregateSharedRevenue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregateSharedRevenue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevShareTermOrCondition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aggregateSharedRevenue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Aggregate revenue shared for a product offering if true. Provide details about each acquisition of an offering if false.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssociationRoleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aggregation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether an association role is a shared or composite aggregation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregationDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aggregationDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TariffUsageProdOfferPriceCharge</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aggregationDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The aggregationDuration specifies the duration during which ProductUsages have to be aggregated before applying the TarifUsageProdOfferPriceCharge globally on the ProductUsages aggregated volume.  The type of this attribute is String as it might be more complex than a simple duration, such as "all ProductUsages between 8AM-8PM during one month".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The action to be invoked when an alarm is triggered [iCalendar] Notes ACTION [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmChangedTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmChangedTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmChangedTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the last date and time when the alarm is changed on the alarm-owning system. Any change to the alarm whether coming from the alarmed resource, or triggered by a change from the client is changing this time.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmClearedTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmClearedTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmClearedTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the time (as a date + time) at which  the alarm is cleared.  Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for alarm clearance.    It is not filled on an alarm for which the clearance has not been received, but it is mandatory for a cleared alarm.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteCalendarAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An absolute date/ time for the alarm to activate</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmEscalation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmEscalation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmEscalation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if this alarm has been escalated or not. Possible values are 0 to 10. A value of zero means no escalation.  The meanings of values 1-10 are to be determined by the user of the interface, but they show increasing levels of escalation.  This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Local identifier of the Alarm. Note that this identifier is local to the server side of the interface, i.e. the alarm-owning system.   Only EntityIdentifier can be considered as global.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmRaisedTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmRaisedTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmRaisedTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the time (as a date + time) at which the alarm occurred.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmReportingTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmReportingTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmReportingTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the time (as a date + time) at which the alarm was reported by the owning system.   It might be different from the alarmRaisedTime. For instance, if the alarm list is maintained by an EMS, the alarmRaisedtime would be the time the alarm was detected by the NE, while the alarmReportingTime would be the time this alarm was stored in the alarm list of the EMS.  This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmSeverityAssignmentList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmSeverityAssignmentList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AlarmSeverityAssignmentProfile</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmSeverityAssignmentList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies a list of Alarm Severity Assignments (ASA). Each record of this sequence specifies the probable cause (plus optionally the probableCauseQualifier and / or the nativeProbableCause) and the severities to be assigned.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmTrigger -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmTrigger">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RelativeCalendarAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmTrigger</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies if the alarm trigger durationOffset relates to the start or the end of the Entry</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alarmType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alarmType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Categorizes the alarm.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aliasNameList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aliasNameList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToBeDeprecated»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aliasNameList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains a list of aliases for the network entity.  See R_TMF518_FMW_I_0001.This attribute contains a list of aliases for the entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aliveDuring -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aliveDuring">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Individual</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aliveDuring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Birth date and death date.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allocatedBudget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allocatedBudget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Budget</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>allocatedBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount allocated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allocationDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allocationDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceAllocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>allocationDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedApiEntities -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedApiEntities">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>allowedApiEntities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A comma separated list of authorised entities for this API.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedOperations -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedOperations">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>allowedOperations</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A comma separated list of authorised operations like POST, PATCH for this API.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedValueTypes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#allowedValueTypes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VariableStandard</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>allowedValueTypes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of string attributes that define the set of class names (which correspond to a set of datatypes) that are allowed to be used in conjunction with this PolicyVariable. Each string provides a class name, which corresponds to a particular subclass of PolicyValue. Each allowed subclass defines an object with a compatible datatype and semantics. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs. The IETF RFCs only define “MATCH”.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alphabetName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alphabetName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Language</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alphabetName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The alphabet name use for the language Note: ISO standard ?</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alternativeDifferences -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#alternativeDifferences">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecAlternativeRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>alternativeDifferences</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A textual description of the differences between the alternates.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountLimited -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountLimited">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ChargeAmountThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>amountLimited</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Limited amount could be affordable by certain BillingAccount.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayComponentSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>amountPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>amountPeriod specifies the duration covered by the amount. For example, the amount may correspond to a complete Year, in this case if the pay is executed monthly, the amount will be devided by 12 to find the amount for one pay.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountRangeInterval -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#amountRangeInterval">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>amountRangeInterval</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies the inclusion or exclusion of the lower range and upper range amount attributes. Possible values are "open", "closed", "closedBottom" and "closedTop".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#apiProtocolType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#apiProtocolType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>apiProtocolType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>API protocol type like REST, SOAP and so on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicabilityLabel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicabilityLabel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicabilityLabel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Label that is used as a guidance to decide applicability / inapplicability</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableCode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableCode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicableCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicator that specifies whether an instance represents applicability or un-applicability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableDays -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableDays">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicableDays</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A day or days representing applicability or inapplicability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableDuring -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableDuring">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicableDuring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Time period during which the applicability or inapplicability needs to be considered</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableStateValues -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicableStateValues">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SapSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicableStateValues</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of possible states that a ServiceAccessPoint may take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicationDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#applicationDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProdOfferPriceAlteration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>applicationDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies for a ProductOfferingPriceAlteration that impacts recurring ProductOfferingPrice the duration of application. For example, the ProductOfferingPriceAlteration may apply 10% discount only during 6 months.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#appliedAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#appliedAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerPaymentItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>appliedAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount of money that has been applied to specific entity, such as CustomerBill.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#appliedDemandAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#appliedDemandAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AppliedCapacityDemand</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>appliedDemandAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An amount of demand applied to a CapacityAmount. Note that this is a composite attribute defined by CapacityAmount.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aristocraticTitle -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#aristocraticTitle">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>aristocraticTitle</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A name that describes someone's aristocratic position, such as Baron, Graf, Earl, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#asapRef -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#asapRef">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>asapRef</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignedPriority -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignedPriority">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>assignedPriority</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order's assigned priority after review.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignedResponsibilityDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignedResponsibilityDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>assignedResponsibilityDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The target response date assigned after review.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignmentPurpose -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assignmentPurpose">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerBillingAccountAssignment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>assignmentPurpose</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates why the BillingAccount is related to the FinancialAccount. For example, for taxes, revenue associated with an invoice, bill, or credit memo, payment, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#associationType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#associationType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleAssociation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>associationType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the association, such as organizational, household, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assumptions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#assumptions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>assumptions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assumptions made when defining the Project (especially assumptions for success)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attachedOnDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attachedOnDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Attachment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>attachedOnDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attackVector -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attackVector">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentAttackMethod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>attackVector</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Attack method chosen from the following enumerated list:  Exploited New Vulnerability Exploited Known Vulnerability Self Propagating Malicious Logic Insider Purposeful Insider Accidental Distributed Network Activity Non Distributed Network Activity Network Scan System Scan Compromise Through Another System Reconnaissance Unknown/NA Other (See Comment)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attribute1 -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#attribute1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CharacteristicSpecValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>attribute1</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#audibleAlarm -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#audibleAlarm">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>audibleAlarm</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this SecureHolder is equipped with an audible alarm. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#audibleAlarmDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#audibleAlarmDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>audibleAlarmDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that provides supplementary information for the AudibleAlarm attribute. It should only be filled in when the value of the AudibleAlarm attribute is TRUE. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#authenticationLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#authenticationLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunicationInteractionRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>authenticationLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CommunicationInteractionRole's authenticationLevel specifies the level of authentication of the PartyRole or ResourceRole. It may impact what the interactor has the right to ask for.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#authenticationType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#authenticationType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>authenticationType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The authentication type like OAUTH, SSL used for this API</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#availability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#availability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpactLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>availability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A loss of availability is the disruption of access to or use of information or an information system.  Enumerated value indicating the impact to availability due to the Security Incident:   Low - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a limited adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A limited adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is noticeably reduced; (ii) result in minor damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in minor financial loss; or (iv) result in minor harm to individuals   Moderate - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a serious adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A serious adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a significant degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is significantly reduced; (ii) result in significant damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in significant financial loss; or (iv) result in significant harm to individuals that does not involve loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   High - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a severe or catastrophic adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A severe or catastrophic adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a severe degradation in or loss of mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is not able to perform one or more of its primary functions; (ii) result in major damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in major financial loss; or (iv) result in severe or catastrophic harm to individuals involving loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   Source:  FIPS 199.  http://csrc.nist.gov/publications/fips/fips199/FIPS-PUB-199-final.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#averagePay -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#averagePay">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>averagePay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Mid point for this Pay Range. This will be defined at global alignment. This field will define the middle point of an amount an employee can get paid that sit in a particular pay range. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backedUpStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backedUpStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>backedUpStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if the Managed Object (related to this alarm) has a back up or has been backed up.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backgroundColor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backgroundColor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SurfaceSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>backgroundColor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A quality such as red, blue, green, yellow, and so forth, for the background of the surface.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backlogItemNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backlogItemNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_BacklogItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>backlogItemNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backplaneIndependent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backplaneIndependent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>backplaneIndependent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this ManagedDevice has independent backplanes that can be managed separately. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backplaneNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#backplaneNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>backplaneNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the number of backplanes that this device has. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#balanceClass -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#balanceClass">
