<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>bookedQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>/bookedQuantity corresponds to the result of a calculation. It is calculated adding all quantity booked through related StockItemRequests still valid.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#border -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#border">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SurfaceSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>border</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The edge or boundary of a surface.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#boxNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#boxNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PoBoxAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>boxNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number or text that represents a post office box number.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#boxType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#boxType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PoBoxAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>boxType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The kind of box number.  For example one at a post office or other location authorized to maintain postal boxes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brand -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brand">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>brand</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The manufacturer or trademark of the specification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brokerCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brokerCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BrokerCoordinationDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>brokerCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between the PolicyBroker and the PolicyServers that it coordinates the actions of. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brokerCoordinationTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#brokerCoordinationTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BrokerCoordinationDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>brokerCoordinationTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this PolicyBroker has the authority to coordinate the actions of this PolicyServer.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#budget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#budget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorksProgram</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>budget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#buildingName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#buildingName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>buildingName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A well known name for a building. Notes: e.g. Telstra house, Parliament house</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#buildNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#buildNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>buildNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the internal identifier for the compilation of this unit of a SoftwareResourceSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#bundleSpecValidFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#bundleSpecValidFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServicePackageBundleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>bundleSpecValidFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a time period in which the use of this particular ServiceBundleSpec is allowed for implementing the associated ServicePackageSpec. The TimePeriod attribute is a complex data type consisting of a TimeStamp to mark the beginning of the TimePeriod and a TimeStamp to mark the end of the TimePeriod.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverImpact -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverImpact">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetDefBusinessValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessDriverImpact</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A textual description of the impact to the business if the metric lags.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverPriority -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverPriority">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetDefBusinessValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessDriverPriority</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A textual description of how important this metric is to the business.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessDriverValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetDefBusinessValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessDriverValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A textual description of business drivers, such as revenue benefit, cost benefit, efficiency, customer experience, time to market, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessInteractionRevisionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date of the revision.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessInteractionRevisionDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that explains the revision, including why the revision was made.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessInteractionRevisionNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique number that identifies the revision.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#businessInteractionRevisionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>businessInteractionRevisionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The significance of the revision, such as major or minor. Permitted Values: Major, Minor</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cableManagementStrategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cableManagementStrategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HolderComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cableManagementStrategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that contains information on how the various cables contained in the Chassis, Rack, or other type of HolderComposite object are connected and bundled. This property contains information to aid in the assembly and service of the cables contained in a SecureHolder object. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cableType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cableType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalConnector</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cableType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and defines the particular type of cable that is attached to this connector. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: RS-232  2: RS-422  3: RS-423  4: RS-449  5: RS-485  6: RS-530  7: V.35  8: X.21  9: 9 um single-mode  10: 62.5/125 um multi-mode  11: USB  to be continued, not done!  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#calculationFrequency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#calculationFrequency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevenueAssuranceParameter</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>calculationFrequency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The rate of occurrence that a value for a parameter is determined. For example, hourly, daily, weekly.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#calendricalSystem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#calendricalSystem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Calendar</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>calendricalSystem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The default calendrical system for the Calendar  Note:  CALSCALE [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#callDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#callDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VoiceCallUsage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>callDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#callType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#callType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VoiceCallUsage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>callType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#canBeOverridden -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#canBeOverridden">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecCharUse</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>canBeOverridden</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that the CharacteristicSpecValues associated with the CharacteristicSpec cannot be changed when instantiating a CharacteristicValue. For example, a bandwidth of 64 MB cannot be changed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#canMixPower -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#canMixPower">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>canMixPower</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that AC and/or DC power supplies can be used in this device. If it is false, then only one or the other can be used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capabilityType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capabilityType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ExternalSystemCapability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capabilityType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Capability type like policy, charging and so on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityAmount</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value and units that define the CapacityAmount, such as 10000 ea, 10B Mb. Instance values are mutually exclusive with From and To capacityAmounts and range interval.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmountFrom -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmountFrom">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityAmount</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityAmountFrom</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The low range value that a CapacityAmount can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmountTo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityAmountTo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityAmount</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityAmountTo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper range value that a CapacityAmount can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityDemand</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityDemandAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value and units that define the CapacityDemand, such as 10000 ea, 10B Mb.  Instance values are mutually exclusive with From and To capacityDemandAmounts and range interval.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmountFrom -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmountFrom">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityDemand</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityDemandAmountFrom</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The low range value that a CapacityDemand can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmountTo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandAmountTo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityDemand</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityDemandAmountTo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper range value that a CapacityDemand can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capacityDemandType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityDemand</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capacityDemandType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies whether the capacity demand is planned, actual or required by.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capDemandRelType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capDemandRelType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityDemandRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capDemandRelType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as aggregation, used to calculate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capitalCostRate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capitalCostRate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capitalCostRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capRelType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capRelType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CapacityRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capRelType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as aggregation, used to calculate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#captureFrequency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#captureFrequency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasure</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>captureFrequency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The frequency of capture for the MetricDefMeasure.  Note:  This may be replaced by a set of entities similar to the Performance Monitoring ABEs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#captureMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#captureMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasure</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>captureMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The method used to capture the Metrics associated with a MetricDefMeasure.    Note:  This may be replaced by a set of entities similar to the Performance Monitoring ABEs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capturePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#capturePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasure</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>capturePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The period during which Metrics associated with a MetricDefMeasure are captured.    Note:  This may be replaced by a set of entities similar to the Performance Monitoring ABEs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardCompatibilityResults -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardCompatibilityResults">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cardCompatibilityResults</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an attribute that is used to store the result of the negotiation process between a Card and its EquipmentHolder to see if they are compatible. This is the result of the isCompatible() method, with the Card being the source and the EquipmentHolder being the target, translated into a textual description.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NationalIdentityCardIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cardNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a NationalIdentityCard used to identify it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cardNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BankCardPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cardNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The identification number of a bank card.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#carrierShipmentID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#carrierShipmentID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ShipmentTracking</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>carrierShipmentID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifier used to communicate with the Carrier in charge of the corresponding StockItemShipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#carrierTrackingUrl -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#carrierTrackingUrl">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ShipmentTracking</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>carrierTrackingUrl</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Url given by the Carrier in charge of the corresponding StockItemShipment to follow the shipment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cashierInfo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cashierInfo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CashPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cashierInfo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A description of the employee who received the cash for payment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#category -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#category">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>category</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A classification of MarketSegments because they share common characteristics. For example a vertical or horizontal MarketSegment. Vertical MarketSegments put a PartyRole in a single segment, while a PartyRole can exist in multiple horizontal MarketSegments</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cceName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cceName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cceName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Unique identifier to system configuration issues in order to facilitate fast and accurate correlation of configuration data across multiple information sources and tools.  The cceName represents a configuration that makes a resource vulnerable.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#certificateNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#certificateNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BirthCertificateIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>certificateNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned birth certificate used to identify it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeableQuantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeableQuantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chargeableQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeableUnit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeableUnit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chargeableUnit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OffCyclePartyBill</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chargeDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A date through which charges previously received by the billing system appear on the bill.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeDateOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeDateOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyBillingCycleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chargeDateOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An offset of a date through which charges previously received by the billing system will appear on the bill. The offset is expressed as number of days with regard to the start of the BillingPeriod.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chargeType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ChargingCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chargeType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of charge like OneTime, Usage, Recurring applied to an offer</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charIsAnExplicitAttribute -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charIsAnExplicitAttribute">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ConfigSpecCharUse</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>charIsAnExplicitAttribute</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies the use of a CharacteristicSpecification is used to assign a value to an explicitly modeled attribute of an entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charRelationshipType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charRelationshipType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecCharUseRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>charRelationshipType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as aggregation, migration, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charSpecSeq -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charSpecSeq">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecCharUseRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>charSpecSeq</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which a CharacteristicSpecification appears within another CharacteristicSpecification that defines a grouping of CharacteristicSpecifications. For example, a grouping may represent the name of an individual. The given name is first, the middle name is second, and the last name is third. The order in which a CharacteristicSpecification appears within another CharacteristicSpecification that defines a grouping of CharacteristicSpecifications.  For example, a grouping may represent the name of an individual. The given name is first, the middle name is second, and the last name is third.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charValueRelationshipType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#charValueRelationshipType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecCharValueUseRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>charValueRelationshipType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship between values, such as aggregation, migration, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.A categorization of the relationship, such as aggregation, migration, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chassisType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#chassisType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chassis</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>chassisType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the type of Chassis that this object is. Values include: 0: Unknown 1: Desktop 2: Low Profile Desktop 3: Pizza Box 4: Mini Tower 5: Tower 6: Portable 7: LapTop 8: Notebook 9: Sub-Notebook 10: Hand Held 11: Docking Station 12: Main System Chassis 13: Expansion Chassis 14: Bus Expansion Chassis 15: Peripheral Chassis 16: Storage Chassis 17: Rack Mount Chassis  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#checkID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#checkID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CheckPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>checkID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The external identification number of a check specified by the Bank.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ciSource -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ciSource">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorIntelligencePartyRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ciSource</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The origin of the CompetitorIntelligence, such as a financial report, press release, or product brochure, gathered by a PartyRole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#classification -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#classification">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>classification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A specification of what the MarketStatistic represents, for example a ProductProgram, ProductPromotion, ProductOffering, Branch, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#className -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#className">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>className</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>clearStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Clear status of the problem.  Clearance of the resource RC alarm or of the underlying alarms or problems does not imply clearance of the problem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearSystemId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearSystemId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>clearSystemId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the id of the system where the user who invoked the clearResourceAlarm operation is located. This might be different from the alarm-owning system.   Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for alarm clearance.    This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearUserId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clearUserId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>clearUserId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the id of the user who invoked the clearResourceAlarm operation.  Note that the automatic AVC notification generation is disabled for this attribute as a specific notification is generated for alarm clearance.    This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clientMACAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#clientMACAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DHCPSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>clientMACAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Media Access Control (MAC) address that was assigned an IP address during this DHCP event.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#closeDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#closeDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CloseCustomerProblemSummary</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>closeDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date in which the CustomerProblem was closed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#code -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#code">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Currency</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>code</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents the code of the currency in the usage for convenience. Generally it is made up of three capital English letters, the first two of which represent the country and the last of which represents the name of the currency. For example, USD represents United State of America Dollar. Usually ISO 4217 is used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#codeModel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#codeModel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>codeModel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The codeModel specifies the type of codification used for the stockItemCode.  Two main types exist: EAN (European Article Numbering) or GTIN (Global Trade Item Numbering). A GTIN consists of a GS1 Company Prefix, an Item Reference Number and a Check Digit.   Each of them is further defined by the length of the number such as EAN 13, GTIN-12 (USA / Canada for individual products), GTIN-13 (Rest of World for Individual products), GTIN-14 (Worldwide for Product groupings).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#collectionPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#collectionPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdhocCollection</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>collectionPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time range of the requested Performance Indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#collectionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#collectionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>collectionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of the collection such as: gauge, commulative, status inspection. Indicators can be produced using these methods.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#color -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#color">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Symbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>color</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A quality such as red, blue, green, yellow, and so forth, that is seen when looking at something.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#comment -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#comment">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>comment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Comment text about the entry Note: COMMENT [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#comments -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#comments">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>comments</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Comments on problem, as a list of comments.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#completionEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#completionEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ClosedLoopActivitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>completionEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A happening that trigger to completion of the activity. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#compositionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#compositionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompositeCriterionCondition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>compositionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionIsCNF -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionIsCNF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conditionIsCNF</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines the condition clause of this PolicyConditionComposite object to be represented in Conjunctive Normal Form (e.g., an And of Ors). If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then the condition clause will be represented in Disjunctive Normal Form. This attribute controls the setting of how multiple condition clauses (as represented by individual PolicyConditionAtomic objects) are treated in the PolicyConditionComposite object. As such, it is different from the attribute PolicyRule.IsCNF, which controls how multiple PolicyConditionComposite objects are treated in a PolicyRule object. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionResponse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionResponse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conditionResponse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that is used to allow a 'standard' definition of a TRUE/FALSE response to be made by an external system attached to the model at this point. This will allow integration with a generalized policy processing engine. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionSequenceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionSequenceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conditionSequenceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a non-negative integer and represents the particular sequence in which this element is parsed as part of the overall policy structure. This will allow a policy engine to reference externally supplied arguments to this object as it is evaluated.  Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. CIM 2.7 has a subset of these values</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conditionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conditionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that can be used to define the type of condition that this instance is checking. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#confidentiality -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#confidentiality">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpactLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>confidentiality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A loss of confidentiality is the unauthorized disclosure of information.  Enumerated value indicating the impact to confidentiality due to the Security Incident:   Low - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a limited adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A limited adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is noticeably reduced; (ii) result in minor damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in minor financial loss; or (iv) result in minor harm to individuals   Moderate - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a serious adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A serious adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a significant degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is significantly reduced; (ii) result in significant damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in significant financial loss; or (iv) result in significant harm to individuals that does not involve loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   High - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a severe or catastrophic adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A severe or catastrophic adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a severe degradation in or loss of mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is not able to perform one or more of its primary functions; (ii) result in major damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in major financial loss; or (iv) result in severe or catastrophic harm to individuals involving loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   Source:  FIPS 199.  http://csrc.nist.gov/publications/fips/fips199/FIPS-PUB-199-final.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompAtomicConfigSpecRel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A prescribed action that is taken for a ConfigurationSpecification that is part of a group (composite).  For example, "assign" a connection termination point to a connection.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRSPData</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configQuantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configQuantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompAtomicConfigSpecRel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents how many of a related ConfigurationSpecification in a group (composite) are to be configured.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompAtomicConfigSpecRel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which a related ConfigurationSpecification that is part of a group (composite) is to be configured.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configSpecRelationshipType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configSpecRelationshipType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ConfigSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configSpecRelationshipType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship between two ConfigurationSpecifications, such as aggregation, migration, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configurationOrder -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#configurationOrder">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>configurationOrder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that provides any order-specific instructions for configuring the set of components that together constitute this PhysicalDevice. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparator -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparator">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelObjective</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceComparator</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An operator that specifies whether a ServiceLevelObjective is violated above or below the conformanceTarget.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparatorLower -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparatorLower">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceComparatorLower</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An operator that when applied on a value specifies whether a threshold is crossed or ceased to be crossed. This operator is used to compare with the conformanceTargetLower.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparatorUpper -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceComparatorUpper">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceComparatorUpper</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An operator that when applied on a value specifies whether a threshold is crossed or ceased to be crossed. This operator is used to compare with the conformanceTargetUpper.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformancePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformancePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelObjective</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformancePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An interval of time during which the conformanceTarget must be measured.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTarget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTarget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelObjective</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceTarget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value used to determine if ServiceLevelObjective is met.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTargetLower -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTargetLower">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceTargetLower</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value used to determine if the threshold is crossed or ceases to be crossed. It represents the Lower limit. The value should be less than the conformanceTargetUpper. The conformance comparators should also be logically defined so as to not lead to a logically impossible condition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTargetUpper -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conformanceTargetUpper">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conformanceTargetUpper</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value used to determine if the threshold is crossed or ceases to be crossed. It represents the Upper limit. The value should be greater than the conformanceTargetLower. The conformance comparators should also be logically defined so as to not lead to a logically impossible condition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#connectionSetupType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#connectionSetupType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreControlPlane</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>connectionSetupType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the setup type of the FRE. It indicates whether the FRE has been established by UNI signalling (SC) or NMS operation (SPC, PC).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#connectorName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#connectorName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CardOnCardDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>connectorName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an object reference to the PhysicalConnector of the hosting Card that this DaughterCard plugs into. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintData -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintData">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>constraintData</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The constraintData attribute is a string that provides a general extension mechanism for representing PolicyConditions that have not been modeled with specific attributes (as specified in this model). The format of this attribute is determined by the OID value stored in the constraintEncoding attribute of this class. The constraintEncoding attribute provides a convenient and simple mechanism by which a Policy Server can determine whether it supports the values stored in an instance of constraintData. If it doesn't recognize any of the OID values in the constraintEncoding attribute, then it will not know how to interpret the data in the corresponding constraintData attributes. The action for the policy decision point to take in case it does not recognize the format of this data could itself be modeled as a PolicyRule, governing the behavior of the Policy Server. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called Constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintEncoding -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintEncoding">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionVendor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>constraintEncoding</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The constraintEncoding attribute is a string that is used to represent an OID that in turn identifies the encoding and semantics of the constraintData attribute in this instance. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called ConstraintEncoding.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraints -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraints">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>constraints</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Constraints that may affect Project success</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#constraintValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessRuleConstraints</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>constraintValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Value that is constraining the business rule</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumingApplicationId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumingApplicationId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MeasurementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>consumingApplicationId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The identifier of the application that produces performance  indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumptionCapacity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumptionCapacity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkSpecFulfillmentRate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>consumptionCapacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Workforce capacity that is required by the work to be done for the location, and that the organization can supply. Unit of the value can be man hour, man day, etc</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumptionPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#consumptionPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ConsumptionSummary</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>consumptionPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The consumptionPeriod corresponds to the period where UsageVolumeBalanceCredits and / or UsageVolumeBalanceDebits and / or AppliedCustomerBillingProductUsageRates have been aggregated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#contactType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#contactType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AccountContact</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>contactType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the relationship of the contact to the account, such as primary, secondary, and emergency contact.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedActionOrder -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedActionOrder">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContainedPolicyActionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>containedActionOrder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an unsigned integer attribute that defines the relative position of this action in relation to the overall sequence of actions that are associated with a given PolicyAction. Smaller integers indicate earlier positions in the sequence. The value "0" has the special semantics of "don't care". This value is not unique. Thus, if two or more attributes have the same value, they may be performed in any order, but they must all be performed at the appropriate place in the overall sequence.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedConditionGroupNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedConditionGroupNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContainedPolicyConditionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>containedConditionGroupNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is used to define the group to which the condition is a part of. It corresponds logical to the position of parentheses used to group condition terms together.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedConditionIsNegated -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#containedConditionIsNegated">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContainedPolicyConditionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>containedConditionIsNegated</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this condition term is negated. The default value for this attribute is FALSE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#content -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#content">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Attachment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>content</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The content is the document that is attached.  "link" and "content" attributes are mutually exclusive.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#contractorNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#contractorNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContractorIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>contractorNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a contractor used to identify it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conversionFactor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#conversionFactor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceSpecIntervalConversion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>conversionFactor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value used to convert one time interval to another time interval. For example a value of 12 converts a five minute interval into an hour interval.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#coolingRequirements -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#coolingRequirements">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedHardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>coolingRequirements</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that specifies the cooling requirements for this ManagedComponents. Specific cooling information is defined by the Cooling association. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#costToBusiness -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#costToBusiness">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductSpecificationCost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>costToBusiness</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The monetary amount that represents the cost.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#count -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#count">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRDocEnd</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>count</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#country -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#country">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Rack</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>country</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the designation of the country for which the Rack is designed. Country code strings are as defined by ISO/IEC 3166. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cpeName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#cpeName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonPlatformEnumeration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>cpeName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CPE Name is represented by a Well Formed Name (WFN) that is bound to a URI, which provides backward compatability with CPE 2.2,  and a formatted string. For further details on CPE refer to NIST IRs 7695-7698.  Notes: "For example, the following represents a CPE WFN definition of Microsoft Internet Explorer 8.0.6001 Beta:  wfn:[part=""a"",vendor=""microsoft"",product=""internet_explorer"", version=""8\.0\.6001"",update=""beta""].   An example of the formatted string binding is:  cpe:2.3:a:microsoft:internet_explorer:8.0.6001:beta:*:*:*:*:*:* and URI binding is: cpe:/a:microsoft:internet_explorer:8.0.6001:beta."</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creationDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creationDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerProblemTask</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creationDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time in which the CustomerProblemTask was created</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creationTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creationTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDetailRecord</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creationTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OffCyclePartyBill</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creditDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A date through which credits previously received by the billing system appear on the bill</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditDateOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditDateOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyBillingCycleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creditDateOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An offset of a date through which credits previously received by the billing system will appear on the bill. The offset is expressed as number of days with regard to the start of the BillingPeriod.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerBillingAccount</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creditLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The maximum amount of money that may be charged on an account.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditRiskRating -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditRiskRating">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyCreditProfile</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creditRiskRating</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer whose value is used to rate the risk of this Party paying late or defaulting versus paying on time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditScore -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#creditScore">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyCreditProfile</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>creditScore</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A measure of a person?s or organization?s creditworthiness calculated on the basis of a combination of factors such as their income and credit history.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#criticalityLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#criticalityLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyPrivacyProfileTypeCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>criticalityLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The criticityLevel specifies a level of criticality for the set of Personal Identifiable Information (PII) defined by RootEntityTypeCharUse.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currencyAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currencyAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currencyAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A current amount used to value the MarketStatistic. Mutually exclusive with the amount attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The latest expected duration before the actual occurrence</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentLength -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentLength">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalLink</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentLength</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the current length of the PhysicalLink in feet. For some connections, such as wireless connections, this property may not be applicable and should be assigned the special value of NULL. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentNumberLicenses -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentNumberLicenses">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleSoftwareLicenseDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentNumberLicenses</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the current number of licenses that have been allotted for this particular OperatingSystem instance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentNumberProcesses -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentNumberProcesses">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleUsesProcessesDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentNumberProcesses</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the current number of processes that can be used by this particular PartyRole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentPortNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentPortNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Protocol</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentPortNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a non-negative integer that defines the port number used by this protocol.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentSalary -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#currentSalary">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceProviderEmployee</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>currentSalary</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The current fixed regular payment, typically paid on a monthly or biweekly basis but often expressed as an annual sum, made by an employer to an employee.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

