</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardInstallStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardInstallStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daughterCardInstallStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the current installation status of this Card's daughter Cards. Note that this defines the status of daughter Cards as viewed by the hosting Card. Status values of individual daughter Cards are defined by attributes in the daughter card itself. Values include:  0: Not Applicable (doesn't have any DaughterCards)  1: All Daughter Cards are installed  2: Some Daughter Cards are installed  3: No Daughter Cards are installed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardOperatingStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardOperatingStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daughterCardOperatingStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the current operating status of this Card's daughter Cards. Note that this defines the operating status of daughter Cards as viewed by the hosting Card. Status values of individual daughter Cards are defined by attributes in the daughter card itself.   This attribute only defines the physical operating characteristics of the daughter card. It does not say whether the daughter Card is functioning correctly, as that is a logical attribute.  Values include:  0: Not Applicable (doesn't have any DaughterCards)  1: All Daughter Cards are operating correctly  2: Some Daughter Cards are operating incorrectly  3: No Daughter Cards are operating correctly</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardRequirements -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daughterCardRequirements">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daughterCardRequirements</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the relationship between this Card and all DaughterCards. Values include:  1: No DaughterCard can be attached  2: Requires 1 or more DaughterCards to function correctly  3: Can optionally use 1 or more DaughterCards</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfMonthMask -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfMonthMask">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dayOfMonthMask</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that refines the definition of the valid time period that is defined by the timePeriod attribute. This is done by explicitly specifying the days of the month when the policy is valid. These attributes work together, with the timePeriod attribute used to specify the overall time period during which the PolicyRule might be valid, and the dayOfMonthMask attribute used to pick out the specific days of the month within that time period when the PolicyRule is valid. This property is formatted as a fixed string of 64 bits. The first 31 bits correspond to the days of the month counting from the beginning, followed by 31 more bits identifying the days of the month counting from the end, followed by 2 bits that are always set to '0'. For each day, the value '1' indicates that the policy is valid for that day, and the value '0' indicates that it is not valid. The value X'80 00 00 01 00 00 00 00', for example, indicates that a PolicyRule is valid on the first and last days of the month. For months with fewer than 31 days, the digits corresponding to days that the months do not have (counting in both directions) are ignored. The encoding of the 62 significant bits in the octet string matches that used for the schedDay object in the DISMAN-SCHEDULE-MIB. If this attribute is not specified, then the PolicyRule is treated as valid for all days in the months specified by the timePeriod attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfWeek -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfWeek">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StandardWorkPeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dayOfWeek</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfWeekMask -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dayOfWeekMask">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dayOfWeekMask</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that refines the definition of the valid time period that is defined by the timePeriod attribute. This is done by explicitly specifying the days of the week when the PolicyRule is valid. These attributes work together, with the timePeriod attribute used to specify the overall time period when the policy might be valid, and the DayOfWeekMask used to pick out the specific days of the week in that time period when the PolicyRule is valid. This property is formatted as a fixed length string of 8 bits. The first 7 bits identify the 7 days of the week, beginning with Sunday and ending with Saturday, followed by 1 bit that is always set to '0'. For each day of the week, the value '1' indicates that the PolicyRule is valid for that day, and the value '0' indicates that it is not valid. If this attribute is not specified, then the PolicyRule is treated as valid for all 7 days in the weeks specified by the timePeriod attribute. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called DayOfWeekMask.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfMonthRecurrence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfMonthRecurrence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MonthlyScheduleDayOfMonthDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daysOfMonthRecurrence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The list of days of month when the monthly schedule definition is active on, e.g. 10th , 15th , 20th.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfWeek -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfWeek">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ApplicableTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daysOfWeek</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A day or days representing when the schedule is applicable.  For example 2, 3 represent Monday and Tuesday.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfWeekRecurrence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#daysOfWeekRecurrence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WeeklyScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>daysOfWeekRecurrence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The list of days of week when the weekly schedule definition is active on: e.g. Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dcOutputPower -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dcOutputPower">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dcOutputPower</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the maximum value of the output power of the DC PowerSupply. If this is an AC PowerSupply, then this attribute must be set to NULL.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#decisionStrategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#decisionStrategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicySetSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>decisionStrategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that specifies the particular decision strategy to be used in this PolicySet.  Permitted Values: 0: Unknown 1: MatchFirst 2: MatchAll MatchFirst enforces the actions of the first rule that evaluates to TRUE; policy evaluation then STOPS, meaning that all subsequent rules are no longer evaluated. MatchAll enforces the actions of all rules that evaluate to TRUE. This is equivalent to performing two passes through the rule set. The first pass gathers all PolicyRules that evaluate to true and places them in a group. The second pass then executes only those rules that evaluated to true. Execution of these rules is controlled through the Priority property (on the aggregation PolicySetComponent), which defines the order in which the PolicyRules execute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#defaultNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#defaultNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>defaultNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Default number of instances of RootEntity according to the type of RootEntityRelationship.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#defaultRelOfferNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#defaultRelOfferNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BundledProdOfferOption</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>defaultRelOfferNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The default of related ProductOfferings that is used to initialise the number of ProductOffering in an order as part of the BundledProductOffering.  The default number must be consistant with the lower and upper limit. It isn't mandatory to specify it and in this case it is considered a default number 0.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#definesExemption -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#definesExemption">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TaxDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>definesExemption</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If TRUE, the TaxDefinition corresponds to a tax exemption that replaces a standard tax if a corresponding TaxExemptionCertificate grants it.  For example, a voluntary organization may be granted a complete exemption from value-added tax, to pay 0% of the standard tax.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#definition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#definition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerabilityTool</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>definition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Defines required signature or policy definition that must be installed on the tool.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#degreeOfCorrelation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#degreeOfCorrelation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorProductCorrelation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>degreeOfCorrelation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A percentage that measures how closely an enterprise's ProductOffering compares to a CompetitorProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#delimiter -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#delimiter">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>delimiter</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A character used to specify the boundary between separate members.  Notes:  For example, ";", ",", ":"</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#delimiterSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#delimiterSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityGroupMemberExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>delimiterSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which a delimiter appears in this part of an expression.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dependencyLag -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dependencyLag">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElementRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dependencyLag</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time lag to be applied to the dependency.  Only applicable if type is Dependency. Notes: May be zero</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dependencyLead -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dependencyLead">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElementRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dependencyLead</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time lead to be applied to the dependency. Only applicable if type is Dependency. Notes: May be zero</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deploymentActivityState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deploymentActivityState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>deploymentActivityState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents the activity state of the current deployment request (e.g. activate, modify, and deactivate). If there is no in-progress deployment request, then the activity state is INACTIVE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deploymentState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deploymentState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>deploymentState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents the state of provisioning of the forwarding relationship between the set of end points.  PARTIAL: Indicates that only part of the FRE has been activated in the network.  PENDING: Indicates that none of the FRE resources have been deployed.  COMPLETE: Indicates the FRE has been successfully deployed in all Network Elements and no further intervention is required.  Note that a COMPLETE FRE is not necessarily enabled to carry traffic or carrying traffic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#depth -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#depth">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>depth</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the depth of the ManagedComponent using the units specified in the MeasurementUnits attribute. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationAlgorithm -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationAlgorithm">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProdOfferPricePolicyVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>derivationAlgorithm</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A reference to a logical sequence of steps for determining the value of the ProdOfferPricePolicyVariable.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationFormula -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationFormula">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>derivationFormula</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A rule or principle represented in symbols, numbers, or letters, often in the form of an equation used to derive the value of a characteristic value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#derivationMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyIndicatorSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>derivationMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>he method used to calculate the value of a AnomalyIndicator, such as average, minimum, maximum, sum, and so forth</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#descriptionExtension -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#descriptionExtension">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetDefDescExtension</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>descriptionExtension</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that represents the extension to the description of MetricDefinition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#desiredSpeed -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#desiredSpeed">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Fan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>desiredSpeed</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer attribute that defines the currently requested fan speed, defined in revolutions per minute.  For non-variable speed Fans, this attribute has the same semantics as turning the Fan on or off. For variable-speed Fans, this attribute represents the desired speed of the Fan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#destinationAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#destinationAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VoiceCallUsage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>destinationAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#detectionMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#detectionMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>detectionMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Method used for detection (e.g. user report, detected by sensor, network flow analysis)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deviceGroupID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#deviceGroupID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>deviceGroupID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string, and is used to uniquely identify this device as a member of a group of devices. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dialectNames -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dialectNames">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Language</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dialectNames</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of the dialects of the language Note: ISO standard ?</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dialedNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dialedNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceNumber</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dialedNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute called dialedNumber exist to specify the number, for any of those types: mobile like MDN, fixed, and IP type of numbers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#directCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#directCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>directCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#directCostRate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#directCostRate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>directCostRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#direction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#direction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyPayment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>direction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The direction of the payment seen by the company. It can be inbound (payment made to the company) or outbound (payment made by the company).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disabilities -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disabilities">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Individual</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>disabilities</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Notes:  Used for legal requirements (special billing, special products, special contact media, such as Braille). This should be modeled as a separate entity but is shown as an attribute for brevity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disclosureDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disclosureDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>disclosureDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time the vulnerability was publicly disclosed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#discoveredDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#discoveredDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>discoveredDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time the vulnerability was discovered.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#discoveredName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#discoveredName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>discoveredName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains the name of the object when its existence is first published on the CCV.  See R_TMF518_FMW_I_0001 and R_TMF518_FMW_I_0003.This attribute contains the name of the object when its existence is first published on the CCV but only in the case where the OS that publishes the object on the CCV is not the naming OS.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disputedAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#disputedAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DAACreated</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>disputedAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount which the customer wants a refund for.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#docId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#docId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRDoc</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>docId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#documentID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#documentID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDetailRecord</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>documentID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#documentNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#documentNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Agreement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>documentNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A reference number assigned to an Agreement that follows a prescribed numbering system.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dueDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dueDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dueDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date upon which the ProductOrder is due for completion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#duplexMode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#duplexMode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalPort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>duplexMode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the duplex mode of this port. Values are:  0: Unknown  1: Full Duplex  2: Half Duplex  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#duration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#duration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorksProgram</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>duration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#durationOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#durationOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RelativeCalendarAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>durationOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies the alarm offset. e.g. -5 mins is 5 minutes before and 10hr is 10 hours after</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dX -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dX">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RelativeLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dX</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The x Cartesian coordinate relative to the referenceLocation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dY -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dY">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RelativeLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dY</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The y Cartesian coordinate relative to the referenceLocation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dynamicAttrAssoc -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dynamicAttrAssoc">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityType</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dynamicAttrAssoc</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies whether dynamic attributes or associations or both have been added for the RootEntityType.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dZ -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#dZ">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RelativeLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>dZ</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The z Cartesian coordinate relative to the referenceLocation. Notes: required for 3D representations</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#effectiveDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#effectiveDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ConsumptionSummary</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>effectiveDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The effectiveDate corresponds to the date where the ConsumptionSummary have been produced.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#effectiveness -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#effectiveness">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerabilityFixAction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>effectiveness</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>States whether the fix action fully avoids the risk associated with the vulnerability or reduces risk to some extent.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#elevation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#elevation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Property</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>elevation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The height above sea level, in the indicated units</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#eMailAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#eMailAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EmailContact</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>eMailAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A full e-mail address in standard format. Notes: e.g. fred.bloggs@thing.com</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#emitConstraint -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#emitConstraint">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventEmitDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>emitConstraint</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a string that contains the specific OCL expression to constrain how a particular Event is emitted by a particular Resource. Defining this as an attribute enables external applications to populate this constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#employeeNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#employeeNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceProviderEmployee</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>employeeNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique identification number for an employee.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#enabled -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#enabled">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContainedPolicySetsDetail</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>enabled</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer. If its value is 1 (which means enabled), then this signifies that this object is enabled for evaluation. If its value is 3 (which means that it is enabled for debugging), then this rule can be used in test or debug scenarios. If its value is 2, then this object is disabled and cannot be used or evaluated. Note that this object still might end up being disabled, even if this attribute is TRUE. For example, an associated PolicyTimePeriodCondition might evaluate to FALSE, effectively disabling this object. That's why the phrasing said "enabled for evaluation" instead of "enabled for use". Values include: 0: Unknown 1: Enabled for evaluation 2: Disabled for use 3: Enabled for debugging</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#encompassingFinancialImpact -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#encompassingFinancialImpact">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpact</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>encompassingFinancialImpact</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Financial impact due to Incident</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endActiity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endActiity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>endActiity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents the action that trips the workflow. Linked to Activity ABE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteraction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>endDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date on which an interaction is closed or completed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>endEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the event signaling end of the workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endpointRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endpointRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityEventEndpoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>endpointRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Defines the role of the endpoint in the Security Event.  Possible enumeration values:  Source, InternalSource, TranslatedSource, or Destination.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#endTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRDocEnd</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>endTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#entryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#entryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>entryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date when MetricDefintion was defined or added.  It is meant to provide an indication of how old the MetricDefinition is.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#entryRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#entryRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryAttendance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>entryRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#epic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#epic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_BacklogItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>epic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#errorEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#errorEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ClosedLoopSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>errorEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies events that signal occurrence of an error.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#estimatedDeliveryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#estimatedDeliveryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ShipmentTracking</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>estimatedDeliveryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date on which the StockItemShipment should be delivered at the final place.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#eventSequenceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#eventSequenceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>eventSequenceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a non-negative integer and represents the particular sequence in which this event is parsed as part of the overall event clause. This will allow a policy engine to reference externally supplied arguments to this object as it is evaluated. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exceptionAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exceptionAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionDeterminationMethod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exceptionAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Action to take when one or more of the related MetricDefinitionMethodArgument cause indeterminate results, such as a denominator of 0 in a ratio or a missing value for a  MetricDefinitionMethodArgument.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exceptionEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exceptionEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exceptionEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies events to signal abnormalities of the workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#excludedDates -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#excludedDates">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ScheduleDefinitionExcludedDates</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>excludedDates</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Dates that should be excluded from the Schedule definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exclusions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exclusions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exclusions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specific exclusions that may have been reasonably expected to be included in the Project</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#excutionPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#excutionPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketingCampaign</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>excutionPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Start date and End date representing the period during which the MarketingCampaign is executed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionConstraints -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionConstraints">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyGroupExecutionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionConstraints</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a string that contains the specific OCL expression to constrain how a given set of PolicyEvents are distributed to a particular PolicyGroup. Defining this as an attribute enables external applications to populate this constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionEndTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionEndTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyGroupExecutionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionEndTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines an end time by which the PolicyEventSet should be executed. If it isn't executed by this time, then the action specified in the ExecutionFailure event of this object should be executed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionFilter -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionFilter">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyGroupExecutionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionFilter</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The ExecutionFilter attribute contains an OCL expression that defines which components in the PolicyGroup this PolicyEventSet will be passed to, so it can be evaluated. It is expected that this attribute is populated by an external application that knows what policy elements are contained in a particular PolicyGroup.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionStartTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionStartTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyGroupExecutionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionStartTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines when the PolicyEventSet should be executed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The execution state of the management job. It is used to indicate a failure in the execution of the job.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionStrategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#executionStrategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>executionStrategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the strategy to be used when executing the sequenced actions aggregated by this PolicyRule. Defined execution strategies include: 0: Unknown 1: Do Until Success 2: Do All 3: Do Until Failure 4: Do All Without Failure or Do Nothing "Do Until Success" means that actions should be executed according to their predefined order, until successful execution of a single action. At that point, the process should stop (even if there are additional actions that could be executed). "Do All" means that all actions should be executed that are part of the set, according to their predefined order. This should continue, even if one or more of the actions fails. "Do Until Failure" means that all actions should be executed according to their predefined order until an action fails to execute. At that point, the entire sequence should be stopped. Finally, "Do All Without Failure or Do Nothing" means that all actions specified should be performed. However, if a failure occurs, then NONE of the actions should be performed. This implies EITHER the ability to look-ahead and ensure that the actions will be able to be performed successfully, or the ability to perform a rollback of that action and all previous actions when an error is encountered.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exerciseDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exerciseDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exerciseDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If the incident is part of an exercise, this attribute describes that exercise.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exitCondition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exitCondition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exitCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the condition to exit from the workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedCompletionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedCompletionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedCompletionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Expected delivery date amended by the provider.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ShipmentCheckPoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date on which the shipment should arrive at this ShipmentCheckPoint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElementSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The normal duration of this standard element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedEquipmentObjectType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedEquipmentObjectType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedEquipmentObjectType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the type of the expected resource. For example, "Fan" or "STM16" for the Equipment class and "Line Shelf" for the Equipment Holder class.) This is an empty string if there is no expected equipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedEquipmentType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedEquipmentType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedEquipmentType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the type of the expected resource. For example, "Fan" or "STM16" for the Equipment class and "Line Shelf" for the Equipment Holder class. This is an empty string if there is no expected equipment. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedOrInstalledEquipmentRef -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expectedOrInstalledEquipmentRef">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expectedOrInstalledEquipmentRef</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the equipment object expected or installed in the equipment holder, if any. Null if the equipment holder is empty or if it only contains other equipment holders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expirationDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expirationDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BankCardPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expirationDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date of card expiration.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exploitPublishedDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exploitPublishedDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exploitPublishedDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time the exploit for the vulnerability was published.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exploitType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#exploitType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityThreatExploit</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>exploitType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An enumerated list of threa exploit types, such as:   Software Flaw  Weak Security Control  Cross-scripting Exploit  User-interaction Dependent Tool</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expression -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expression">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Intent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expression</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An Intent contains a set of expectations expressed  (expression) in statements using a particular espressionLanguage. This attribute captures the intent expressed by the TM Forum Intent Ontology (TIO) as is stored as  a string. The expression is the formal statement of the intent and contains all the information that describes the complete intent.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expressionLanguage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#expressionLanguage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Intent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>expressionLanguage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Determines the language used to express intent. E.g JSON-LD, Turtle.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#extensible -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#extensible">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>extensible</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that the values for the characteristic can be extended by adding new values when instantiating a characteristic for an Entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#extensionDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#extensionDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ScheduledDuration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>extensionDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The duration of the expected extensions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalRepresentationReference -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalRepresentationReference">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TransmissionDescriptor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>externalRepresentationReference</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute provides a means to store at the target OS a reference to the external representation of the Transmission Descriptor.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalSchema -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalSchema">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>externalSchema</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The external API schema of the (external) url offered to the client of this API.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalUrl -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#externalUrl">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>externalUrl</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The url of an API offered to the user. this is seen as external url for an API brokerage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyGeneration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyGeneration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>familyGeneration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An abbreviation or word that pertains to the generation in a family, such Sr, Jr.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyNamePrefix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyNamePrefix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>familyNamePrefix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Notes: e.g. Van den, Von etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyNames -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#familyNames">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>familyNames</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains the non-chosen or inherited name. Also known as a person's last name in the Western context. Notes: Also known as surname  Multiple fields may be entered with a delimiter in-between</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fieldId -->

