<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fieldName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionAccountType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionAccountType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyCreditProfileReference</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>financialInstitutionAccountType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of financial institution account.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionAccoutNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionAccoutNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyCreditProfileReference</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>financialInstitutionAccoutNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The financial institution account number that identifies the party account at the financial institution.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#financialInstitutionName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyCreditProfileReference</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>financialInstitutionName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The name of the financial institution that holds the referenced account.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#firstAlert -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#firstAlert">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>firstAlert</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that indicates what first alerted the system to the problem. It is not the root cause of the Service Problem.  Examples:  Threshold crossing alert: Service component causing the problem  Customer report: customer name (or TT id) reporting the problem</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fixActionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fixActionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerabilityFixAction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fixActionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An enumeration of to describe the type of fix action. Enumeration values:   Mitigation - mitigates the potential impact from an exploit of the vulnerability   Remediation - removes the vulnerability from the affected resource.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fixedScheduleStartTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fixedScheduleStartTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FixedScheduleItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fixedScheduleStartTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date & time to start a job/activity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flags -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flags">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetFlowSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>flags</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Flags set in packet headers</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flowIdentifier -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flowIdentifier">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreConnectionless</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>flowIdentifier</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This parameter contains the internal identifier of the flow through TPEs and decomposed FREs.  An example of a flow identifier is the IVID which defines the value to be used for VID in S-TAGs pushed onto the frames at entry to the FD.  When the value of flowIdentifier on an FRE is not “null", the value of the  corresponding flowIdentifier for all of the TPEs attached to this FRE and to any supporting FREs have the same value as the as the flowIdentifier on the FRE.  If the FRE is performing flowIdentifier swapping inside (as opposed to only at the edges), the flowIdentifier on the FRE is not meaningful (and set to “null”).  Note:  Since the flowIdentifier a TPE of the FRE has the same value as the flowIdentifer of the FRE (when the flowIdentifier of the FRE is not “null”) any attempt to set a different value for the flowIdentifier of the TPE will be rejected.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flowIDHeaderNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#flowIDHeaderNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv6FlowIDVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>flowIDHeaderNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that defines the particular packet header that contains the IPv6 flow ID information. Specifying the packet header is necessary in case the address is tunneled. In this case, it is mandatory that the correct address be chosen for comparison. Values are: 0: outermost header 1: next innermost header 2: second innermost header etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#followedBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#followedBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntityIdentificationSpecFormat</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>followedBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>One or more characters that follow the EntityIdentification value. For example, the format of a phone number contains dashes, such as 972-477-8401.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#forecastBudget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#forecastBudget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Budget</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>forecastBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount forecasted.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#format -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#format">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>format</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the specific revision format used in this version. Each field of the revision is separated by a period. For example, if the desired format is .>, then the value of this string could be: major-number.minor-number The semantics of the format should be described in the revisionSemantics attribute of this class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formattedName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formattedName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>formattedName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains, in one string, a fully formatted name with all of its pieces in their proper place. This includes all of the necessary punctuation. This de-normalized form of the name cannot be easily parsed. Note: if NULL, then derive from the other fields using name policy</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formFactor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formFactor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chip</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>formFactor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the form factor of this PhysicalComponent. Values include: 0: Unknown 1: Other 2: Custom 3: SIP 4: DIP 5: ZIP 6: SOJ 7: SIMM 8: DIMM 9: PGA 10: RIMM 11: SRIMM 12: SODIMM 13: SOIC 14: LCC 15: PLCC  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formOfAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formOfAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>formOfAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains the Salutation,e.g. Mr., Mrs., Hon., Dr.,Major, etc Note: Also known as person title Also includes. Miss, Ms,</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formula -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#formula">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SalesCommissionSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>formula</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A rule or principle represented in symbols, numbers, or letters, often in the form of an equation used to derive the value of SalesCommission.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#freeBusyType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#freeBusyType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>freeBusyType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Determines the event resource reservation on the Calendar Notes: TRANSP, FREEBUSY, FBTYPE [iCalendar] Permitted Values: FREE, BUSY, BUSY-UNAVAILABLE, BUSY-TENTATIVE</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#frequency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#frequency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SalesOpportunity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>frequency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Frequency of Revenue</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#freType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#freType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>freType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute provides the name of the type of the FRE.  The type is an expression of the traffic flow and potential for flow (accounting for protection switching constructs etc) through the FRE between the EndPoints of the FRE.  This attribute essentially provides the name of the spec for the FRE. The FRE may have further specification details provided via other specification mechanisms.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#from -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#from">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GoalDirection</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>from</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Source of goal achievement. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fromToDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fromToDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ApplicableTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fromToDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The period of time for which Capacity or CapacityDemand applies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fromValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fromValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristicValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fromValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The low range value that a characteristic can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FulfilmentCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fulfilmentID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The unique identifier of a fulfilment capability offered by a fulfillment system.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FulfilmentCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fulfilmentType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of a fulfilment capability offered by a fulfillment system.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fulfilmentVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FulfilmentCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fulfilmentVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The version of a fulfilment capability offered by a fulfillment system.This may include subfileds like major and minor which are separated by a period delimiter.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fullAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#fullAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>fullAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A denormalised string showing the type and position numbers up the hierarchy with separator characters. Notes: provide if required for performance purposes. e.g. SUITE 5 /  RACK 7B / SUBRACK 2 / CARD 3</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#functionalArea -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#functionalArea">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_Impediment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>functionalArea</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#functionalPurpose -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#functionalPurpose">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ASIC</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>functionalPurpose</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the functional purpose of this ASIC. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Routing Traffic  2: Forwarding Traffic  3: Encrypting Traffic  4: Firewalling  5: Encoding  6: General Computational Functions</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gender -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gender">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalConnector</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>gender</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the gender type of the connector. Values are:  0: Unknown  1: Not Applicable  2: Male  3: Female  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#generation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#generation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>generation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An abbreviation or word that pertains to the generation in a family history, such as Sr., Jr., III (the third), and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#geometry -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#geometry">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GeographicLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>geometry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The two dimensional graphical representation of the Location allowing it to be displayed on a map and to be used for spatial calculations. Notes: Since Geometry is abstract, the attribute will actually be one of the concrete subclasses</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#givenNames -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#givenNames">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>givenNames</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Note: Also known as Christian name, chosen name, first name  Multiple fields may be entered with a delimiter in-between or stored in a collection</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#GMTSessionEndDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#GMTSessionEndDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>GMTSessionEndDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#GMTSessionStartDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#GMTSessionStartDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>GMTSessionStartDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gracePeriods -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gracePeriods">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelObjective</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>gracePeriods</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The number of times an objective can remain un-updated without a violation of a ServiceLevelAgreement in reference to a measurement period and/or ServiceLevelAgreement reporting period.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#granularity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#granularity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>granularity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the granularity at which the indicator is evaluated for threshold crossing.  If the threshold applies to a single indicator, then this attribute is mandatory. It can only be omitted for complex threshold involving multiple indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridX -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridX">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GridLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>gridX</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The grid x coordinate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridY -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridY">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GridLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>gridY</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The grid y coordinate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridZ -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#gridZ">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GridLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>gridZ</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The grid z coordinate. Notes: not normally used</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#groupNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#groupNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionRuleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>groupNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is used to define the group to which the condition is a part of. It corresponds logical to the position of parentheses used to group condition terms together.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#handlingState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#handlingState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Intent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>handlingState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A enumerated list of states, including StateIntentReceived, StateCompliant, StateDegraded, StateFinalizing</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#handOfActivity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#handOfActivity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>handOfActivity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents the point of interface outbound from the workflow. Linked to Activity ABE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hardwarePurpose -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hardwarePurpose">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedHardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hardwarePurpose</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the purpose of the ManagedHardware. Values include:  1: Required  2: Optional  3: Redundant  4: Fail-Over  5: Other  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hardwareVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hardwareVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hardwareVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that contains the hardware version number of this Card.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasActiveCooling -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasActiveCooling">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CoolingDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasActiveCooling</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean that, if TRUE, means that this CoolingDevice provides active cooling. If it is false, then cooling is provided by a passive means.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasAdapter -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasAdapter">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Slot</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasAdapter</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this slot has an adapter installed that enables it to accept other types of cards (e.g., fitting an adapter on two Slots enable them to accept a Card that otherwise could not be accommodated). If its value is FALSE, then no adapter is present. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasEvaluated -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasEvaluated">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasEvaluated</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that is set by a policy application to define the state of evaluation of this PolicyCondition.   Permitted Values: 0: not yet evaluated 1: evaluated as TRUE 2: evaluated as FALSE Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasEventEvaluated -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasEventEvaluated">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyEventBase</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasEventEvaluated</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that is set by a policy application to define the state of evaluation of this event. Values include: 0: not yet evaluated 1: evaluated as TRUE 2: evaluated as FALSE</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasExecuted -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasExecuted">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasExecuted</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that is set by a policy application to define the state of execution of this policyAction.   Permited Values: 0: not yet executed 1: executed with no errors 2: executed with errors but successfully rolled back 3: executed with errors and did not roll back 4: did not complete execution but successfully rolled back 5: did not complete execution and did not roll back  Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasMultipleQoSTypes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasMultipleQoSTypes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceBundle</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasMultipleQoSTypes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this ServiceBundle as containing more than a single type of QoSService (e.g., DiffServ and 802.1P as an example).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasStarted -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasStarted">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Service</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasStarted</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this Service has already been started. If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then this signifies that this Service has NOT been Started.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubActions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubActions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasSubActions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this PolicyAction has one or more sub-actions. Sub-actions are used to enforce a hierarchical nesting of actions, so that parent actions may control the evaluation and other semantics of the sub-actions that they contain.  Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubPolicyActions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubPolicyActions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasSubPolicyActions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this PolicyAction has one or more sub-actions. Sub-actions are used to enforce a hierarchical nesting of actions, so that parent actions may control the evaluation and other semantics of sub-actions that they contain. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubRules -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hasSubRules">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleBase</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hasSubRules</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this PolicyRule has one or more sub-rules. Sub-rules are used to enforce a hierarchical nesting of rules, so that parent rules may control the execution and other semantics of sub-rules that they contain.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#header -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#header">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRSPData</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>header</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#heatGeneration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#heatGeneration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chassis</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>heatGeneration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the amount of heat generated by the Chassis in BTU/hour. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#height -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#height">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>height</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the height of the ManagedComponent using the units specified in the MeasurementUnits attribute. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#heightInUs -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#heightInUs">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Rack</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>heightInUs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the height of the Rack in 'U's. A 'U' is a standard unit of measure for the height of a Rack or rack-mountable components. It is equal to 1.75 inches or 4.445 cm. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#holderStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#holderStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>holderStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute, based on M.3100, indicates the status of the EquipmentHolder. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Installed And Acceptable  2: Installed And Not Acceptable  3: Not Installed  4: Mismatch Of Installed and Acceptable  5: Unavailable  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hostNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hostNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hostNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This contains the host number portion of the IP Address.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hotSwappable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#hotSwappable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalContainer</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>hotSwappable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that defines whether it is possible to replace this object instance with a physically different, but equivalent, object instance while the containing Equipment has power applied to it. TRUE means that it is HotSwappable, and FALSE means that it is not.  All HotSwappable PhysicalComponents are inherently Removable and Replaceable.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Unambiguously distinguishes different object instances.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ifType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ifType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalPort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ifType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and specifies the particular media type of the link. This attribute provides additional detail beyond that provided in the ifType of an ifEntry of a MIB (e.g., distinguishing between 10Base and 100Base ethernet). Values include:  0: Unknown 1: 10BaseT 2: 100BaseT 3: 10-100BaseT 4: 1000BaseT 5: 10000BaseT 6: DS-0 7: DS-1 8: DS-3 9: OC-3 10: OC-12 11: OC-48 12: OC-192  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#impactImportanceFactor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#impactImportanceFactor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>impactImportanceFactor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Impact Importance is characterized by an Impact Importance Factor: overall importance of the impact of all the affected services, e.g. 0 (zero impact) to 100 (worst impact). The Impact Importance is a calculated field which is set by the OSS determining the impact.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#impactPattterns -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#impactPattterns">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>impactPattterns</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define the patterns of impact (optional)  - e.g. other service characteristics  - Used when defining impact through another pattern than the pre-defined attributes above  This field is extendable.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#incidentCause -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#incidentCause">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentAssessment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>incidentCause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Free text description of the cause of an intrusion</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#includesResourcesUseByAnotherFre -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#includesResourcesUseByAnotherFre">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MultiRouteManagement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>includesResourcesUseByAnotherFre</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates whether one (or more) of the component FREs of the route or TPEs  associated directly with an component FRE of the route is carrying traffic of another FRE, i.e. is involved in another route that is active, (True) or not (False).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inclusions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inclusions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inclusions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Items that the Project covers that are not obvious</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorCategory -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorCategory">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceIndicatorSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indicatorCategory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A grouping or set of PerformanceIndicatorSpecifications that are classified together because of common characteristics, such as technology specific, service specific, or technology/service independent.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indicatorName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the  name of performance indicator, KPI, gauge or counter which crossed the threshold.   If the threshold applies to a single indicator, then this attribute is mandatory. It can only be omitted for complex threshold involving multiple indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyIndicatorSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indicatorType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A kind of value that the AnomalyIndicator can take on, such as numeric, text, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorUnit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indicatorUnit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indicatorUnit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the unit of the measurement of the indicator corresponding to the threshold that has been crossed in a free format string.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indirectCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indirectCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indirectCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indirectCostRate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#indirectCostRate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>indirectCostRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#initialDetectionDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#initialDetectionDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>initialDetectionDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date/time initial detection of activity occurred associated with this incident.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputCurrentMax -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputCurrentMax">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputCurrentMax</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the input current rating in amperes for a fully populated chassis. For a DC PowerSupply, this is the maximum current drawn when operating at the lowest permissible value of its input voltage range. For an AC PowerSupply, the value of this attribute is the same as the value of the InputCurrentMin attribute.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputCurrentMin -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputCurrentMin">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputCurrentMin</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the input current rating in amperes for a fully populated chassis. For a DC PowerSupply, this is the minimum current drawn when operating at the lowest permissible value of its input voltage range. For an AC PowerSupply, the value of this attribute is the same as the value of the InputCurrentMax attribute.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputOctets -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputOctets">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputOctets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputSource -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputSource">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputSource</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies source of input to the workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputVoltageHigh -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputVoltageHigh">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputVoltageHigh</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the high value for the Input Voltage Range for this PowerSupply.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputVoltageLow -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inputVoltageLow">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inputVoltageLow</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the low value for the Input Voltage Range for this PowerSupply.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installationOrder -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installationOrder">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chassis</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installationOrder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that defines the order of installation of components into the Chassis. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedEquipmentObjectType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedEquipmentObjectType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedEquipmentObjectType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the type of the installed resource. For example, "Fan" or "STM16" for the Equipment class and "Line Shelf" for the Equipment Holder class.) The installed equipment type is invariant for the lifetime of the hardware. This is an empty string if there is no expected equipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedEquipmentType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedEquipmentType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedEquipmentType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the type of the installed resource. For example, "Fan" or "STM16" for the Equipment class and "Line Shelf" for the Equipment Holder class. The installed equipment type is invariant for the lifetime of the hardware. This is an empty string if there is no installed equipment. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedPartNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedPartNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedPartNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the vendor's resource Part Number (PN) of the installed equipment. If PN is not available empty string shall be used. If the part and serial number are both non-null then the part+serial number together shall be unique.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedSerialNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedSerialNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedSerialNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains the vendor's serial number of the installed equipment. Unique, if no default is provided. At least one serial number has to be provided.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedTimeStamp -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedTimeStamp">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServicePlaceDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedTimeStamp</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time a Service has been installed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installedVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installedVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the vendor's resource version of the installed equipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installSize -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installSize">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installSize</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount and units, such as 800 MB, required to install the SoftwareResource.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#installStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>installStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an m.3100 attribute that represents the availability of the type of Equipment that this object represents. Its semantics are as follows.  The attribute availability status is used to indicate whether the correct physical piece of equipment (in m.3100, it is called a "circuit pack") is isntalled or not. This is a set valued attribute and includes the values notInstalled and empty. If the type of the inserted physical circuit pack matches the value of the circuitPackType attribute (relating to the circuitPack instance) then the value of the availabilityStatus is an empty set. Otherwise, the value of the availabilityStatus attribute is notInstalled even if it is one of the acceptable circuit pack type  This is implemented as an enumerated integer. The values will include at least the following:  0: Unknown  1: Operational (installed and matches expected type)  2: Installed (buit does not match expected type)  3: Not Installed  4: In Maintenance  5: Failed  6: Not operational  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#integrity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#integrity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpactLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>integrity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A loss of integrity is the unauthorized modification or destruction of information.  Enumerated value indicating the impact to integrity due to the Security Incident:   Low - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a limited adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A limited adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is noticeably reduced; (ii) result in minor damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in minor financial loss; or (iv) result in minor harm to individuals   Moderate - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a serious adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A serious adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a significant degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is significantly reduced; (ii) result in significant damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in significant financial loss; or (iv) result in significant harm to individuals that does not involve loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   High - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a severe or catastrophic adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A severe or catastrophic adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a severe degradation in or loss of mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is not able to perform one or more of its primary functions; (ii) result in major damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in major financial loss; or (iv) result in severe or catastrophic harm to individuals involving loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   Source:  FIPS 199.  http://csrc.nist.gov/publications/fips/fips199/FIPS-PUB-199-final.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#interactionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#interactionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GeographicLocationRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>interactionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of relationship between the locations. This could be a binary topological relationship type (touches, crosses, overlaps, equals, contains, within) if a spatial engine is not available and the spatial relationships are being modeled directly, or some more general relationships.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#internalSchema -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#internalSchema">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>internalSchema</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The internal API schema of the (internal) url which an API broker uses.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#internalUrl -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#internalUrl">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>internalUrl</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The url of an API offered to an API brokerage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#interval -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#interval">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceSpecificationInterval</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>interval</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value that represents the period of time over which the PerformanceSpecificaion is collected.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#intervalTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#intervalTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Performance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>intervalTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The increment of time (including date) for which the associated PerformanceIndicators were calculated/determined.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#intiallyReportedDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#intiallyReportedDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>intiallyReportedDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date and time initially reported.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalConnector</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inUse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this PhysicalConnector is in use by some other component of the system. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inventoryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#inventoryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemStockLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>inventoryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date of the last inventory of the StockItemStockLevel</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#involvementType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#involvementType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevenueSharingModelInvolvement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>involvementType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The specification of whether revenue is retained by an enterprise and whether a party participates in revenue sharing. For example, an enterprise may charge a listing fee for a party's offering or offerings as part of an agreement between a party and an enterprise, and an enterprise passes all revenue on to the party for sales of the party's offering. The party is invoiced separately for the listing fee. For a template revenue sharing model only an enterprise's involvement is specified. When a party enters into a revenue sharing agreement and a template is used their involvement is specified.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAC -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isAC</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies this to be an AC PowerSupply. If FALSE, then it is a DC PowerSupply.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAlarmReporting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAlarmReporting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isAlarmReporting</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies whether alarm reporting for this FRE is administratively enabled or disabled.   True = alarm reporting is enabled; False = alarm reporting is disabled.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAppointmentRequired -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isAppointmentRequired">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isAppointmentRequired</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies if this kind of work requires an appointment with the customer/owner to be performed at their location</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isCNF -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isCNF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleBase</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isCNF</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines the condition clause of this rule to be represented in Conjunctive Normal Form (e.g., an AND of ORs). If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then the condition clause will be represented in Disjunctive Normal Form (e.g., an OR of ANDs).  This attribute controls the setting of how multiple condition clauses (as represented by multiple PolicyConditionComposite objects) are treated in the PolicyRule. As such, it is different from the attribute PolicyConditionComposite.IsCNF, which controls how multiple PolicyConditionAtomic objects are treated in a (single) PolicyConditionComposite object.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isComposite -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isComposite">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDevice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isComposite</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this physical device is in reality made up of a set of physical devices, each of which can be individually managed. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConfigurable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConfigurable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalComponent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isConfigurable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this PhysicalComponent is configurable by the end-user. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConfigurablePhysically -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConfigurablePhysically">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isConfigurablePhysically</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this Card has one or more options that can be physically configured. Each of these options has a distinct physical manifestation (e.g., additional memory, or faster CPU) that usually (but not always) results in occupying more room in the Card.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConsumable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isConsumable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isConsumable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDefault -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDefault">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristicValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isDefault</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if the value is the default value for a characteristic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDistributable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDistributable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isDistributable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, designates the SoftwareResource as being able to be distributed across multiple physically distinct Resources.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDistributedCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isDistributedCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isDistributedCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this SoftwareResource as being currently distributed across several Resource nodes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgeFlowIdentifierPreserved -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgeFlowIdentifierPreserved">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreConnectionless</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEdgeFlowIdentifierPreserved</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If True, the relevant flow identifier of particular information egressing the FRE at the boundary of the FRE is the same as the flowIdentifier used for that particular traffic at the ingress to the FRE. If flowIdentifier stacking or translation is applied within the FRE, the stacking/translation tables on all endpoints of the FRE will be set such that the above condition is satisfied for any flow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgePriorityPreserved -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgePriorityPreserved">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreConnectionless</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEdgePriorityPreserved</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute shall indicate whether the egress Priority in the frame header must be the same as the ingress Priority</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgeResourcePort -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEdgeResourcePort">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourcePort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEdgeResourcePort</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute. If the value of this attribute is TRUE, then this ResourcePort is located at the edge of a Network or SubNetwork.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEnabled -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEnabled">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FieldDescriptor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEnabled</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEphemeral -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEphemeral">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Protocol</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEphemeral</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute. If its value is TRUE, then this protocol can use ephemeral port numbers. If its value is FALSE, then this protocol will only use well-defined port numbers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEquipmentProtected -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isEquipmentProtected">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TerminationPointEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isEquipmentProtected</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates whether or not the TPE is supported by a protected Equipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExactAlternative -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExactAlternative">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecAlternativeRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isExactAlternative</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies if the alternate is an exact alternate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExercise -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExercise">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isExercise</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether this incident is real or part of an exercise (i.e. part of a test of an organization's security posture).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExperimental -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isExperimental">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isExperimental</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute. If the value of this attribute is TRUE, then this represents a special build (perhaps as a trial to suit specific customer needs).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isFalsePositive -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isFalsePositive">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isFalsePositive</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Boolean for the evaluation whether this incident is a false positive or not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isFixed -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isFixed">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isFixed</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies whether the FRE can be deleted via the interface (isFixed = FALSE) or cannot be deleted (isFixed = TRUE).   Where isFixed = TRUE attempts to delete the FRE by the OS will be rejected.  Where an FRE has a route (i.e. is known to traverse multiple NEs) all NFREs of the FRE must be fxed for the FRE to be fixed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isIntendedRoute -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isIntendedRoute">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MultiRouteManagement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isIntendedRoute</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates whether this route is the intended (prefered) route of the FRE (True) or not (False).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLegalEntity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLegalEntity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Organization</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isLegalEntity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Permitted Values: TRUE or FALSE</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLocalTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLocalTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isLocalTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that the times represented in the timePeriod attribute and in the various Mask attributes represent local times. If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then this means that the times represented in the timePeriod attribute and in the various Mask attributes represent UTC times. There is no provision for mixing of local times and UTC times: the value of this attribute applies to all of the other time-related attributes. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called LocalOrUtcTime.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLocatedAt -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isLocatedAt">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServicePlaceDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isLocatedAt</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A indicator that specifies if a Service has been installed at the Location.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatory -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatory">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Service</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isMandatory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this Service is mandatory (i.e., this Service must be running when the managed environment is in a non-failed state). If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then this means that this Service is not required to run.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatoryASIC -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatoryASIC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ASIC</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isMandatoryASIC</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this ASIC is mandatory for the correct operation of the PhysicalResource that contains it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatoryEvaluation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMandatoryEvaluation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicySet</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isMandatoryEvaluation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that evaluation (and possibly action execution) of this entity is mandatory and must be attempted. If the Mandatory property value of this entity is FALSE, then the evaluation of this entity is considered to be "best effort" and may be ignored.  Notes:  Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMinUnit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMinUnit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CurrencyUnit</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isMinUnit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A flag to indicate if it is minimum unit of a currency.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMotherBoard -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isMotherBoard">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isMotherBoard</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this Card as either a motherboard or another type of hosting board. When FALSE, it isn't.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isNegated -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isNegated">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionRuleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isNegated</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this condition is negated. The default value for this attribute is FALSE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#iso2Code -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#iso2Code">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Country</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>iso2Code</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>ISO 2 letter country abbreviation. Notes: refer ISO-3166</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#iso3Code -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#iso3Code">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Country</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>iso3Code</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>ISO 3 letter country abbreviation Notes: refer ISO-3166</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isOnCriticalPath -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isOnCriticalPath">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SimpleActivity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isOnCriticalPath</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if the Activity is on the Project critical path</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isOperational -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isOperational">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LogicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isOperational</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is used to define the operational status of the object, and is implemented as a Boolean: TRUE means that the object is currently operational, and FALSE means that the object is not currently operational.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPackage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPackage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecCharUse</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isPackage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that the associated CharacteristicSpecification is a composite.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPhysicalEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPhysicalEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventEmitDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isPhysicalEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, identifies this event as being emitted from a PhysicalResource. If it is FALSE, then this event has been emitted from a LogicalResource.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPluggable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPluggable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CardOnCardDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isPluggable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a Boolean that, if TRUE, means that this DaughterCard can "plug into" its hosting Card without any external cabling. FALSE means that this DaughterCard requires an external cable to attach it to its hosting Card. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPromotion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isPromotion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isPromotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>isPromotion specifies if the ProductOffering is a promotion to encourage Parties to buy, rent, or in some other way procure the offering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRedundant -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRedundant">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isRedundant</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies this PowerSupply as a redundant PowerSupply.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isReportingAlarms -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isReportingAlarms">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isReportingAlarms</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute provides an indication of whether alarm reporting for this Equipment is enabled (true) or disabled (false).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isReservable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isReservable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isReservable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRSVPEnabled -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRSVPEnabled">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RSVP</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isRSVPEnabled</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this RSVPService instance is enabled.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRVSPRequested -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isRVSPRequested">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isRVSPRequested</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If an RSVP is expected Notes: RVSP [iCalendar] Permitted Values: True, False</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSellableStandAlone -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSellableStandAlone">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSellableStandAlone</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If TRUE indicates that the ProductOffering, which is part of a BundledProductOffering, can also be offered for sale stand-alone, if FALSE means that the ProductOffering can only be sold within a BundledProductOffering. NOTE: This attribute only applies to offerings that are part of a BundledProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isServiceEnabled -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isServiceEnabled">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Service</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isServiceEnabled</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, signifies that this Service has been enabled for use. If the value of this attribute is FALSE, then this means that this particular Service has NOT been enabled for use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isShared -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isShared">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UsageVolumeProductSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isShared</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>True if the UsageVolumeProductSpec can be shared by several NetworkProducts.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSolitary -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSolitary">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalCapacityDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSolitary</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this ManagedComponent as containing only one PhysicalCapacity. If this is FALSE, then this ManagedComponent contains multiple PhysicalCapacities (all different, of course). This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSolitaryHolder -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSolitaryHolder">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSolitaryHolder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this EquipmentHolder as containing only one ManagedComponent. If this is FALSE, then this EquipmentHolder contains nested ManagedComponents. This is a REQUIRED attrinbute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isStateful -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isStateful">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Service</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isStateful</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this Service can be changed without affecting any other services.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isStdUnit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isStdUnit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CurrencyUnit</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isStdUnit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A flag to indicate if it is standard unit of a currency.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#issueDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#issueDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>issueDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date that the identification was produced / printed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#issuingCountry -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#issuingCountry">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PassportIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>issuingCountry</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The country issuing the passport.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSwitching -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSwitching">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerSupply</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSwitching</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this PowerSupply is a switching (vs linear) PowerSupply.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSymmetricalAlternative -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSymmetricalAlternative">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecAlternativeRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSymmetricalAlternative</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies whether one SoftwareResourceSpecification is an alternate for the other involved in the relationshp and the other is an alternate for the SoftwareResourceSpecfication, or the SoftwareResourceSpecification is an alternate for the other only.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSymmetricConstraint -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isSymmetricConstraint">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecConstraintRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isSymmetricConstraint</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies if the relationship is from  the perspective of just one specification or from both.  For example, A constrains B, and B constrains A.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUniquePhysical -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUniquePhysical">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isUniquePhysical</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, defines this Card to be physically different from other Cards of the same type and therefore requires a special slot. The unique aspects of this Card are described in the UniqueRequirementsPhysical attribute. An example might be a different form factor than other Cards of its type, or the ability to set jumpers on the Card to control its functionality (e.g., clocking).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUsageMonitoring -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUsageMonitoring">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkProductSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isUsageMonitoring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A NetworkProductSpec might be monitored or not. The wording monitored means that the user can’t realise a type of usage if he hasn’t any FixedVolumePackageProd for this type of usage (i.e. without an empty balance). In this case, the attribute isUsageMonitoring is TRUE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUsingHomeRoute -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUsingHomeRoute">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreControlPlane</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isUsingHomeRoute</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates whether the Connection is currently using the home route or not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUTCTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isUTCTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isUTCTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this Software uses absolute (or UTC) time. If FALSE, then it uses LOCAL time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isVariableSpeed -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isVariableSpeed">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Fan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isVariableSpeed</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this fan supports variable cooling speeds. If it is FALSE, then this fan only provides a single cooling speed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isVirtualizable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isVirtualizable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HostingPlatformRequirementSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isVirtualizable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The attribute isVirtualizable specifies if the Capacity required can be virtualized or not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWfSupplierEmployeePool -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWfSupplierEmployeePool">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforceEmployeePool</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isWfSupplierEmployeePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether this pool is managed by the workforce provider company, or by a 3rd-party contractor</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWfSupplierResourcePool -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWfSupplierResourcePool">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforceResourcePool</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isWfSupplierResourcePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether this pool is managed by the workforce provider company, or by a 3rd-party contractor</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWireless -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWireless">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalLink</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isWireless</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that defines whether this link is a wireless connection or not. TRUE means that this is a wireless connection, and FALSE means that the connection uses one or more cables and connectors to communicate. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWorkingPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#isWorkingPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SpecialWorkPeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>isWorkingPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ituArcStateAndStatusList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ituArcStateAndStatusList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ituArcStateAndStatusList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>See R_TMF518_NRB_I_0001 and R_TMF518_NRB_I_0004.   See supporting document SD1-8_encodingX731M3100...\..\Framework\SD\SD1-8_encodingX731M3100.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ituStateAndStatusList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ituStateAndStatusList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonResourceInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ituStateAndStatusList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>See R_TMF518_NRB_I_0001 and R_TMF518_NRB_I_0004.   See supporting document SD1-8_encodingX731M3100...\..\Framework\SD\SD1-8_encodingX731M3100.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#jobId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#jobId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>jobId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The ID of the management job.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#jobPriority -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#jobPriority">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>jobPriority</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The priority of the management job. The way the management application will use the JobPriority to schedule job execution is application specific and outside of the scope.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#keywords -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#keywords">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Policy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>keywords</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines a set of one or more keywords that a policy administrator may use to assist in characterizing or categorizing a policy object to facilitate search operations. The following keywords are pre-defined:  Permitted Values:   Unknown InstallPermissions  ConfigChange InstallMethod  Default Error  Usage InternalError  Security ExternalError  Authentication Notification  Authorization Publish  Accounting Subscribe  Auditing Publish-Subscribe  Service Exception  CustomerFacingService   ResourceFacingService  Notes: Not present in the ITU specs; the CIM defines a PolicyKeyword attribute, but its semantics are very different.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#keyWords -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#keyWords">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceFunctionSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>keyWords</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of key words that may help in searches to find an RF spec with desired capabilities</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#landCover -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#landCover">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Property</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>landCover</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The vegetation (natural or planted) or man made constructions (buildings, etc.) which occur on the earth surface. Water, ice, bare rock, sand and similar surfaces also count as land cover. [Land Use Database]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#landUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#landUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Property</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>landUse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A series of operations on land, carried out by humans, with the intention to obtain products and/or benefits through using land resources. [Land Use Database]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastModifiedDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The DateTime (in UTC time) that the entry was lastModifier Note: LAST-MODIFIED [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastModifiedDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The last date and time the vulnerability was updated</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastModifiedTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastModifiedTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Defines the time when the management job was last modified.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastStartTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastStartTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastStartTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a TimeStamp that defines the last time that this Sofware was started.  A TimeStamp is a complex attribute that contains a Date and a Time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastUpdateDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastUpdateDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastUpdateDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Last date/time the incident was updated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastUsed -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lastUsed">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lastUsed</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date when the MetricDefinition was last used (in a report, study, and so forth).  This attribute provides a quick reference as to how useful the metric is over time.  If the lastUsed data is many years old, then the suggestion is that the MetricDefinition may not be as useful as it once was.  No value means no use of this MetricDefinition has been made thus far, thus making it more of a hypothetical MetricDefintion whose utility has not been demonstrated.  This is derived based on its use as described above.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#layerProtocolName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#layerProtocolName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>layerProtocolName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the name and potentially additional information such as version number for the protocol/layer that the FRE supports. Syntax and semantic to be specified.  Note: allowed value examples: “X2”, “LR Optical Channel”.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#layerProtocolNameList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#layerProtocolNameList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkForwardingDomain</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>layerProtocolNameList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Each entry provides the name and potentially additional information such as version number for (one of) the protocol(s)/layer(s) that the NFD supports. Syntax and semantic to be specified.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#leaseDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#leaseDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DHCPSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>leaseDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time duration that the IP address has been assigned to the MAC address for.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#legalName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#legalName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>legalName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains, in one string, a fully formatted name with all of its pieces in their proper place. This includes all of the necessary punctuation Note: if NULL, then derive from the other fields using name policy</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#legalPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#legalPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Organization</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>legalPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Incorporation date to disincorporation date.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#length -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#length">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ComponentEntityIdentificationSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>length</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The value that represents unit of measure for the ComponentEntityIdentificaitonSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#level -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#level">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>level</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Describes the place the MarketStatistic holds in a hierarchy of MarketStatistics. For example, director, executive, external, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#levelNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#levelNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>levelNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number used where a level type may be repeated e.g. BASEMENT 1, BASEMENT 2. Notes: some level Types do not require a level Nr e.g.  BASEMENT, LOWER GROUND, MEZZANINE, UPPER GROUND</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#levelType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#levelType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>levelType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The level types within a building. Notes: e.g. BASEMENT, FLOOR, LOWER GROUND, LEVEL, MEZZANINE, UPPER GROUND</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#licenseNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#licenseNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DriversLicenseIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>licenseNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a driver's license used to identify it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#licenseValidityTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#licenseValidityTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleSoftwareLicenseDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>licenseValidityTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a time period for which this license for this particular OperatingSystem is valid.  A TimePeriod is a complex attribute, consisting of a Date and a TimeStamp for the starting period of the license and a Date and a TimeStamp for the ending period of the license.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lifeCycleStage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lifeCycleStage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorProductCorrelation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lifeCycleStage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The stage in the life cycle of the ProductOfferings being correlated. Examples are acquisition, retention, win back, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lifecycleStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lifecycleStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Catalog</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lifecycleStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The condition of the catalog, such as active,testing, published</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lineStyle -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lineStyle">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LineSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lineStyle</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The appearance of the line, such as dashed or dotted.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lineWidth -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lineWidth">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LineSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lineWidth</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The width of a line.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#link -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#link">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Attachment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>link</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A kind of unique resource identifier like a file path or url that points to location of the attachment.  "link" and "content" attributes are mutually exclusive.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#linkageReference -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#linkageReference">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionCategory</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>linkageReference</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A reference to other forms of categorization such as Frameworx domains or Business Architecture domains.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#listeningProficiency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#listeningProficiency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LanguageAbility</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>listeningProficiency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Degree of mastery in listening to a language.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locality -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locality">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>locality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>"An area of defined or undefined boundaries within a local authority or other legislatively defined area, usually rural or semi rural in nature." [ANZLIC-STREET], or a suburb "a bounded locality within a city, town or shire principally of urban character " [ANZLIC-STREET]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#localOrientation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#localOrientation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalCoordinateSystem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>localOrientation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The orientation of the LocalCoordinateSystem, such as directional (north, south) or facing (front, back,side), angle of rotation from the axes of the LocalCoordinateSystem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locationInChassis -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locationInChassis">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ChassisPosition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>locationInChassis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Some Racks have movable "shelves" that Chassis can fit into. In order to identify the position that the Chassis occupies, a pair of measurements - number of Us from the top of the Rack and number of Us from the left side of the Rack - are provided as a comma-delimited string. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locationRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#locationRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteractionLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>locationRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The locationRole specifies the role of the location (i.e. related Place) for the BusinessInteraction or BusinessInteractionItem. For example, it can be "installation" when related to a PartyOrderItem.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lockPresent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lockPresent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lockPresent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that this SecureHolder is protected by some type of lock. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#logData -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#logData">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalySecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>logData</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text from logs that captured information relevant to the event.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#logo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#logo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Logo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>logo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Logo of Organization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lotNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lotNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Property</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lotNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a Property lot that is used to identify it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lowerSize -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lowerSize">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SegmentSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lowerSize</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The lowerSize specifies the targeted minimum size of the calculated Segment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lrStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#lrStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LogicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>lrStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer whose value indicates the current status of the object. The following values are defined:  0: Unknown  1: OK  2: Initializing  3: Starting  4: Paused  5: Stopping  6: Stopped  7: Degraded  8: Stressed   9: Predicted Failure  10: Error - General  11: Error - Non Recoverable  12: Not Installed or Not Present  13: In Maintenance  14: Unable To Contact  15: Lost Communications  Stopped indicates that the LogicalResource is known to still exist, but it is no longer operational. However, it has not failed.  Stressed indicates that the LogicalResource is functioning, but needs attention (e.g., it may be overheating, or overloaded in some way). This is similar to Predicted Failure, which indicates that this LogicalResource is functioning properly, but is predicting a failure in the near future.  In Maintenance indicates that this LogicalResource is being configured, maintained, or otherwise administered and is NOT available for service.  Unable To Contact indicates that the monitoring system has knowledge of this LogicalResource but has never been able to establish communications with it. In contrast, Lost Commmunications indicates that the LogicalResource has been contacted successfully in the past and is known to still exist; however, it is currently unreachable.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NACSecurityEventSubject</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>macAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Media Access Control address of the device considered for network access</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macAddressList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macAddressList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MACVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>macAddressList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an unordered list of strings, each specifying a MAC address or a range of MAC addresses. The 802 MAC address canonical format is used: MACaddress = 1*4HEXDIG ":" 1*4HEXDIG ":" 1*4HEXDIG MACmaskedaddress = MACaddress","MACaddress Each string entry is either: 1. A single MAC address. Example: 0000:00A5:0000 2. A MACmaskedaddress address range defined specified by an address and mask. The mask specifies the relevant bits in the address. Example: 0000:00A5:0000, FFFF:FFFF:0000  defines a range of MAC addresses in which the first 4 8-bit  bytes are equal to 0000:00A5</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macDirection -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macDirection">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MACVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>macDirection</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines if this variable is used to represent source addresses, destination addresses, or both.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macFormat -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macFormat">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MACAddressValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>macFormat</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines how the MAC Address is represented. Values are: 0: a single address (e.g., 0000:00A5:0000) 1: an address with mask (e.g., 0000:00A5:0000, FFFF:FFFF:0000)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macValueList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#macValueList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MACAddressValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>macValueList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of strings, each of which contains a MAC Address. Each string must be of the same format, which is specified in the macFormat attribute of this object.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mailingDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mailingDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OffCyclePartyBill</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mailingDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A party bill mailing date.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mailingDateOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mailingDateOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyBillingCycleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mailingDateOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An offset of a party bill mailing date. The offset is expressed as number of days with regard to the start of the BillingPeriod.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maintenanceVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maintenanceVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maintenanceVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This a string attribute that defines the maintenance number component of the version of SoftwareResourceSpecification. For example, if the version is 3.1.10, the maintenance version is 10.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#majorVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#majorVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>majorVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This a string attribute that defines the major number component of the version of the SoftwareResourceSpecification. For example, if the version is 3.1.10, the major version is 3.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managedObjectClass -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managedObjectClass">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>managedObjectClass</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies, in terms of object class, the resource that is in alarm.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managementMethodCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managementMethodCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>managementMethodCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the particular type of management method that is currently being used.  Permitted Values: 0: Unknown 1: None 2: CLI 3: SNMP 4: TL1 5: CMIP 6: Proprietary Notes:No analog in M.3100 or the DMTF CIM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managementMethodSupported -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#managementMethodSupported">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>managementMethodSupported</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of integers that define the different management methods that are supported by this object.  Permitted Values: 0: Unknown 1: None 2: CLI 3: SNMP 4: TL1 5: CMIP 6: Proprietary Notes: No analog in M.3100 or the DMTF CIM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mandatory -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mandatory">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionDimensionUse</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mandatory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether this dimension is mandatory for this use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manner -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manner">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GoalStrategy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>manner</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manufactureDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manufactureDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>manufactureDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the date of manufacture of this item in the fixed format "dd/mm/yyyy". This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manufacturer -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#manufacturer">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>manufacturer</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the equipment manufacturer name. It is defined as a non-empty free format string with no semantics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maritalStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maritalStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Individual</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maritalStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Permitted Values: married, never married, divorced, widowed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#marketedBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#marketedBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>marketedBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies if the PartyRoleProductOffering is marketed by the related PartyRole.  For example a Competitor PartyRole may only have this attribute set to true and the other boolean attributes set to false.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PaymentPlan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The maximum amount of the Payment when at least one PaymentMethod is declared so that the company generates each Payment. For example, with a due debt of $250, and a maxPaymentAmount of $100, 2 payments of $100 will be generated and the last one will be $50.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxCardinality -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxCardinality">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxCardinality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The maximum number of instances a CharacteristicValue can take on. For example, zero to five phone numbers in a group calling plan, where five is the value for the maxCardinality.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxDataWidth -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxDataWidth">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxDataWidth</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the maximum bus width of this Card. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Special  8: 8 bit data bus  16: 16 bit data bus  24: 24 bit data bus  32: 32 bit data bus  64: 64 bit data bus  128: 128 bit data bus  The value "1" can be used for any non-standard data bus width.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxExtensions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxExtensions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ScheduledDuration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxExtensions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The maximal number of expected extensions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximum -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximum">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalMemoryCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maximum</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the maximum amount of memory, in Kbytes, that can be supported by this ManagedHardware instance. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreControlPlane</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maximumCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a number that indicates the maximum cost allowed for an FRE. The cost of an FRE is calculated based on the cost of the supporting links. This link cost represents a vector of one or more metrics, each of which indicates the relative desirability of a particular link over another during path selection.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumLength -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumLength">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalLink</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maximumLength</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the maximum allowable length of the PhysicalLink in feet. For some connections, such as wireless connections, this property may not be applicable and should be assigned the special value of NULL. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maximumNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Mzximum number of instances of RootEntity according to the type of RootEntityRelationship.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumPay -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maximumPay">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maximumPay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maximum pay for this Pay Range. This will be defined at global alignment. This field will define the maximum amount an employee can get paid that sit in a particular pay range. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxNumberLicenses -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxNumberLicenses">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleSoftwareLicenseDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxNumberLicenses</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the maximum number of licenses that be allotted for this particular OperatingSystem instance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxNumberProcesses -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxNumberProcesses">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleUsesProcessesDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxNumberProcesses</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the maximum number of processes that can be allocated to a particular PartyRole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxPowerSupplies -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxPowerSupplies">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxPowerSupplies</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the maximum number of power supplies that can be installed in the Equipment. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxTrialTimes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#maxTrialTimes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PaymentPlan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>maxTrialTimes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Maximum number of trial to submit a payment if it has been rejected.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mcType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mcType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketingCampaign</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mcType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of a MarketingCampaign, such as new or re-launch.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#meanExtensions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#meanExtensions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ScheduledDuration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>meanExtensions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The mean number of expected extensions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#measureDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#measureDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricMeasureGroup</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>measureDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies the date and time of the MetricMeasureGroup.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#measurementUnits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#measurementUnits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>measurementUnits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the MeasurementUnits for the Depth, Height, and Width attributes of this object. Values include:  0: Unknown (or not measured)  1: inches  2: feet  3: millimeters  4: centimeters  5: meters  This is an optional attribute. However, if any of the Depth, Height, or Width attributes are defined, then this attribute is REQUIRED.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mediaType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mediaType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalLink</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mediaType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and is used to define the particular type of media that is used to carry communication. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Wireless  2: Cat1  3: Cat2  4: Cat3  5: Cat4  6: Cat5  7: 50-ohm Coaxial  8: 75-ohm Coaxial  9: 100-ohm Coaxial  10: Fiber-optic  11: UTP  12: STP  13: Ribbon Cable  14: Twinaxial  15: Optical 9um  16: Optical 50um  17: Optical 62.5um  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memberSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memberSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityGroupMemberExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>memberSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which a RootEntityGroupMember appears in this part of an expression.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memorySize -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memorySize">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FlashDisk</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>memorySize</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the size of the Flash disk in MBytes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memoryType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#memoryType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalMemoryCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>memoryType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and defines the type of memory that this ManagedHardware object instance can have. Values include:  O: Unknown  1: DRAM  2: Synchronous DRAM  3: Cache DRAM  4: RAM  5: SRAM  6: VRAM  7: EDRAM  8: EDO  9: ROM  10: PROM  11: EPROM  12: EEPROM  13: FEPROM  14: CDRAM  15: 3DRAM  16: SDRAM  17: SGRAM  18: RDRAM  19: Flash  20: DDR  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#message -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#message">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ShipmentCheckPoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>message</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Message to be communicated to the contact</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metDefType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metDefType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetDefDescExtension</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>metDefType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Type of description extension, such as comments, MetricDefinition owner notes, references, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureApplicability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureApplicability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>metricDefMeasureApplicability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a MetricDefMeasureApplicability is part of the MetricDefMeasureExpresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureConsequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureConsequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>metricDefMeasureConsequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a MetricDefMeasureConsequence is part of the MetricDefMeasureExpresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureThresholdRule -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricDefMeasureThresholdRule">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>metricDefMeasureThresholdRule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a MetricDefMeasureThresholdRule is part of the MetricDefMeasureExpresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#metricLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>metricLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a MetricDefnition based on the importance enterprise-wide.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mgmtInfoValidFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mgmtInfoValidFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mgmtInfoValidFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the time period that this management information is valid for. A TimePeriod is a complex datatype, that has a starting time and an ending time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#middleNames -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#middleNames">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>middleNames</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Middle name(s) or initial(s) Note: Multiple fields may be entered with a delimiter in-between or stored in a collection</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mimeType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mimeType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Attachment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mimeType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A technical characterization of the attachment content format using IETF Mime Types such as mp4 for audio, bmp, gif jpeg for image.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minCardinality -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minCardinality">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minCardinality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The minimum number of instances a CharacteristicValue can take on. For example, zero to five phone numbers in a group calling plan, where zero is the value for the minCardinality.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimum -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimum">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalMemoryCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minimum</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the minimum amount of memory, in Kbytes, that can be supported by this ManagedHardware instance. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimumNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimumNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minimumNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Minimum number of instances of RootEntity according to the type of RootEntityRelationship.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimumPay -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minimumPay">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minimumPay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Minimum pay for this Pay Range. This will be defined at global alignment. This field will define the minimum amount an employee can get paid that sit in a particular pay range. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minorVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minorVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minorVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This a string attribute that defines the minor number component of the version of SoftwareResourceSpecification. For example, if the version is 3.1.10, the minor version is 1.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minVersionForUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#minVersionForUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CFSSpecVersionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>minVersionForUse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the minimal version of this CustomerFacingServiceSpecification to use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Test</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indication of whether the test is running in "PROACTIVE" or "ONDEMAND" mode</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#modelNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#modelNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResourceSpecAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>modelNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that represents a manufacturer-allocated number used to identify the general type and/or category of the hardware item. This, in combination with the PartNumber and the VendorName, identify different types of hardware items. The SerialNumber can then be used to differentiate between different instances of the same type of hardware item. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#modifier -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#modifier">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PlacePhysicalResourceAssoc</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>modifier</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A limitation or qualification of the association.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monitoredObjectClass -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monitoredObjectClass">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MonitoredClassCriteria</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>monitoredObjectClass</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A  monitored object class for specifying the set of instances that are referenced by a PM query.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monitoredObjectInstances -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monitoredObjectInstances">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MonitoredInstancesCriteria</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>monitoredObjectInstances</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of object identifiers for specifying what monitored objects need to be referenced by a PM query.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monthlyDaysOfWeekInstance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monthlyDaysOfWeekInstance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MonthlyScheduleDayOfWeekDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>monthlyDaysOfWeekInstance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The instance of a selected day in the monthly schedule definition, 1-5 or "last" instance. For example: the 2nd Monday in a month.This works in conjunction with the daysOfWeek attribute Permitted Values: 1-4, last</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monthOfYearMask -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#monthOfYearMask">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyConditionTimePeriod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>monthOfYearMask</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The monthOfYearMask attribute is a string that refines the definition of the valid time period that is defined by the timePeriod attribute. This is done by explicitly specifying the months when the policy is valid. Thus, the timePeriod attribute is used to specify the overall time period during which the policy might be valid, and the monthOfYearMask attribute is used to pick out the specific months within that time period when the PolicyRule is valid. This attribute consists of a fixed string of 16 bits. The first 12 bits correspond to the 12 months of the year, beginning with January and ending with December. The last 4 bits are always set to "0". For each month, the value "1" indicates that the policy is valid for that month, and the value "0" indicates that it is not valid. If this attribute is not specified, then the PolicyRule is treated as valid for all twelve months. Notes: Not present in the ITU specs. The CIM defines a similar attribute called MonthOfYearMask.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#motive -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#motive">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityThreatActor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>motive</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A description of the motives ascribed to a given threat.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mountingOptions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mountingOptions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HolderComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mountingOptions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated 16-bit unsigned integer that defines how Equipment in this entity is mounted. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Stand-alone  2: Rack-mounted, free access  3: Rack-mounted, restricted access  4: Enclosed in another chassis  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mtosiSpecificAlarmAttributes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#mtosiSpecificAlarmAttributes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>mtosiSpecificAlarmAttributes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute groups wireline specific alarm attributes coming from MTOSI.  It is present to ease migration from MTOSI RTM implementation and can be considered as conditional for MTOSI.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#multiplicity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#multiplicity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssociationRoleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>multiplicity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that specifies how many instances of RootEntityType can be involved in an association role.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nameOnCard -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nameOnCard">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BankCardPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nameOnCard</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The name of the person who owns the card.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nameType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nameType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OrganizationName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nameType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Co., Inc., Ltd., Pty Ltd. , Plc., Gmbh</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#namingOsRef -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#namingOsRef">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>namingOsRef</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents an identifier for the steward of the object.  See R_TMF518_FMW_I_0001.This attribute represents an identifier for the steward of the object, intended as the OS that sets the name of the object. The namingOS attribute is set by the OS that is responsible for setting the "name" of the object.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nationality -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nationality">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Individual</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nationality</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Note: Pointer to a country object</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nativeEmsName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nativeEmsName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nativeEmsName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains the native EMS Name of the object. It represents how an EMS user addresses an object on the EMS GUI. Its aim is to provide a "nomenclature bridge" for relating information presented on NMS displays and EMS displays (via GUI cut through).  The EMS may or may not support changing this value.This attribute contains a list of aliases for the entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#navigable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#navigable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssociationRoleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>navigable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that indicates if navigation can be made to a RootEntityType involved in an association.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrConsumedAssets -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrConsumedAssets">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunityMember</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nbrConsumedAssets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Number of assets consumed from the Community</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrContributions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrContributions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunityMember</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nbrContributions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Number of assets provided to the Community</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrOfMembers -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrOfMembers">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Community</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nbrOfMembers</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The number of members committed to the community</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrRelatedMembers -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nbrRelatedMembers">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunityMember</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nbrRelatedMembers</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Number of associated CommunityMembers</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#needsLoyaltyAccount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#needsLoyaltyAccount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LoyaltyProgramProdSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>needsLoyaltyAccount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If TRUE, a LoyaltyAccount is needed for each LoyaltyProgramProduct created according to the LoyaltyProgramProdSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeLowerAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeLowerAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>negotiableRangeLowerAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The lower negotiable limiit for an amount.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeLowerQuantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeLowerQuantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>negotiableRangeLowerQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The lower negotiable limiit for a quantity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeUpperAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotiableRangeUpperAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>negotiableRangeUpperAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper negotiable limit for an amount.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotialbleRangeUpperQuantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#negotialbleRangeUpperQuantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>negotialbleRangeUpperQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper negotiable limiit for a quantity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkAccessDomain -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkAccessDomain">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonResourceInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>networkAccessDomain</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains a free-format string used to associate the resource to a Network Access Domain.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkInd -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkInd">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformancePointCode</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>networkInd</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#networkNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>networkNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This contains the network number portion of the IP Address.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkForwardingDomain</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nfdLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute expresses the level  of the NFD in the hierarchy of NFDs</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkForwardingDomain</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nfdRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies purpose for the grouping provided by the NFD.  The NFD could be:  - ROUTING_AREA  - FORWARDING_AREA  - ADMINISTRATIVE_AREA</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nfdType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkForwardingDomain</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nfdType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute  provides the name of the type of the NFD. The type is an expression of the contained topology.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nickName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nickName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Avatar</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nickName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Nick name used to welcome when connecting.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#normalDays -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#normalDays">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyIndicatorSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>normalDays</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Normal values of the AnomalyIndicator used for training the AI/Model</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#normalDaysDataSource -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#normalDaysDataSource">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyIndicatorSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>normalDaysDataSource</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Data source URL where the normal values of the AnomalyIndicator used for training the AI/Model is stored</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#notes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#notes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerabilityFixAction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>notes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>General notes on the SecurityVulnerabilityFixAction</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nrDecimals -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nrDecimals">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ComponentEntityIdentificationSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nrDecimals</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value that represents the number of digits in the ComponentEntityIndentificationSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nrDigits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#nrDigits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ComponentEntityIdentificationSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>nrDigits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value that represents the number of digits in the ComponentEntityIndentificationSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#number -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#number">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductSpecificationVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>number</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents the occurrence of the version in the sequence of versions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfAllowedCrossing -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfAllowedCrossing">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfAllowedCrossing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The number of allowed crossing occurrences in reference to the tolerancePeriod without a consequence being initiated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfBytes -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfBytes">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetFlowSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfBytes</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Total number of bytes captured in a network flow</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfChassisSlots -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfChassisSlots">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chassis</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfChassisSlots</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the number of Slots that are in the Chassis. This does NOT account for any SlotAdapters used - these are described by the CardInSlot association. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfDevicesCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfDevicesCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDeviceComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfDevicesCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the current number of PhysicalDevices aggregated by this PhysicalDeviceComposite object that are active and manageable.  Note that this aggregation is for that particular level of aggregation. Thus, if a PhysicalDeviceComposite, called A, contains another PhysicalDeviceComposite, called B, then B's instance of this attribute will define how many PhysicalDevices are aggregated by B, whereas A's instance of this attribute will defined how many PhysicalDevices are aggregated by A (which includes those aggregated by B).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfDevicesTotal -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfDevicesTotal">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalDeviceComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfDevicesTotal</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the total number of PhysicalDevices aggregated by this PhysicalDeviceComposite object. Note that this aggregation is for that particular level of aggregation. Thus, if a PhysicalDeviceComposite, called A, contains another PhysicalDeviceComposite, called B, then B's instance of this attribute will define how many PhysicalDevices are aggregated by B, whereas A's instance of this attribute will defined how many PhysicalDevices are aggregated by A (which includes those aggregated by B).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfPackets -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberOfPackets">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetFlowSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberOfPackets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Total number of packets in the network flow</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberProcessActiveTotal -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberProcessActiveTotal">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberProcessActiveTotal</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer attribute that defines the maximum number of total processes that a SoftwareSpecifciation can support at any given time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberProcessesActiveCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberProcessesActiveCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberProcessesActiveCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer attribute that defines the current number of total processes that the Software can support at any given time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelCatLowerLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelCatLowerLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceCatSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberRelCatLowerLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The lower limit of the number of PerformanceCategories that can related. Values can range from 0 to unbounded.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelCatUpperLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelCatUpperLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceCatSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberRelCatUpperLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper limit of the number of PerformanceCategories that can related. Values can range from 0 to unbounded.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelOfferLowerLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelOfferLowerLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BundledProdOfferOption</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberRelOfferLowerLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The lower limit of related ProductOfferings that can be procured as part of the BundledProductOffering.  Values can range from 0 to unbounded.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelOfferUpperLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numberRelOfferUpperLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BundledProdOfferOption</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numberRelOfferUpperLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper limit of related ProductOfferings that can be procured as part of the BundledProductOffering.  Values can range from 0 to unbounded.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numOfIPs -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numOfIPs">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceIPAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numOfIPs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents the number of IP addresses specified by a range of IP Addresses in the ipAddress attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numUsersCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numUsersCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numUsersCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a non-negative integer that defines the current number of users of the Sofware.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numUsersMax -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#numUsersMax">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>numUsersMax</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a non-negative integer that defines the maximum number of users for a SoftwareSpecifciation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#objectInstanceFilter -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#objectInstanceFilter">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MonitoredClassCriteria</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>objectInstanceFilter</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A filter that can be used in conjunction with the  monitored object class for specifying the set of instancesthat are referenced by a PM query.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#observationPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#observationPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricMeasurementObservation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>observationPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Period during wich the observation (measurements) are done.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#observedValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#observedValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>observedValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the observed value: the value of the indicator which crossed the threshold.  This may be different from the threshold value if, for example, the indicator is a gauge and this gauge only takes on discrete values.  If the threshold applies to a single indicator, then this attribute is mandatory. It can only be omitted for complex threshold involving multiple indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offCycleProductionReason -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offCycleProductionReason">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OffCyclePartyBill</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>offCycleProductionReason</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The reason for this off cycle run reason, values may be CUSTOMER_REQUEST, ACCOUNT_CLOSE or others</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ChargingCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>offerID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The identifier of an offer like a mobile service for which this charging capability applied.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerLowerLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerLowerLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BundledProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>offerLowerLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The attribute offerUpperLimit specifies the maximum number of ProductOfferings that can be ordered in the BundledProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerUpperLimit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#offerUpperLimit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BundledProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>offerUpperLimit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The attribute offerLowerLimit specifies the minimum number of ProductOfferings that must be ordered in the BundledProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operationalState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operationalState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceAccessPoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operationalState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether the set of resources supporting the service are installed and working.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operator -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operator">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operator</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A mathematical symbol, term, or other entity that describes an operation.  Notes:  For example, case of, *, /.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorAccess -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorAccess">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyAppliesToDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operatorAccess</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the access privileges that a user (human or otherwise) has when performing various operations on a ManagedEntity residing in a specific PolicyDomain.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorConstraint -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorConstraint">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OperatorConstraintDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operatorConstraint</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a string that contains the specific OCL expression to define which PolicyOperators are allowed to be used in this particular PolicyStatement. Defining this as an attribute enables external applications to populate this constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operatorSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityGroupMemberExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operatorSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which an operator appears in this part of an expression.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#operState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyReport</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>operState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Operational state of associated Anomaly </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#opType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#opType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyOperator</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>opType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that specifies the various types of operators that are allowed for this PolicyStatement.  Permitted Values: 1: Match 2: Greater than 3: Greater than or equals 4: Less than 5: Less than or equals 6: Equals 7: Not equals 8: IN 9: NOT IN 10: SET 11: CLEAR Notes:  Not present in the ITU or CIM specs. The IETF RFCs only define “MATCH”.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#order -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#order">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionRuleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>order</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an unsigned integer attribute that defines the relative position of this action in relation to the overall sequence of actions that are associated with a given PolicyRule. Smaller integers indicate earlier positions in the sequence. The value "0" has the special semantics of "don't care". This value is not unique. Thus, if two or more attributes have the same value, they may be performed in any order, but they must all be performed at the appropriate place in the overall sequence.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderItemAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderItemAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecificationAction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>orderItemAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The corresponding order item action like Add, Modify, Disconnect if this item is orderable.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Collection</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>orderMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and is used to define the method by which elements in an OrderedSet or Sequence are collated. If the Collection type is Set or Bag, then this attribute MUST have the value 1 ("Not Applicable"). Values include:  1: Not Applicable  2: Ascending  3: Descending</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderTakenBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orderTakenBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>orderTakenBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that the associated PartyRole takes an order for the ProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#organizationRoleName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#organizationRoleName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforceOrganizationRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>organizationRoleName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Name of the OrganizationRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orientation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#orientation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>orientation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The angle of rotation from the axes of the local coordinate system.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#originatingSytem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#originatingSytem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>originatingSytem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates where the problem was generated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#originationAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#originationAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VoiceCallUsage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>originationAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#otherDesignator -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#otherDesignator">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>otherDesignator</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute, and enables the manufacturer to label this software as having some set of special restrictions (e.g., early or limited deployment, end of life, or targeted at a specific type of market.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#otherIdentifier -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#otherIdentifier">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>otherIdentifier</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that is used to contain other important identifying data, such as a bar code, of the hardware item. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outbreakDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outbreakDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DunningCaseRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>outbreakDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The outbreakDate represents the date at which the condition of the DunningRule has been verified, triggering the outbreak of the DunningCaseRule.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputDestination -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputDestination">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>outputDestination</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>identifies a destination for the output of a workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputFormat -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputFormat">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdhocCollection</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>outputFormat</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The file format that is used for transferring the performance data between applications.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputOctets -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#outputOctets">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>outputOctets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overall -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overall">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpactLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>overall</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An enumerated value indicating the overall impact to confidentiality, integrity, and availability due to the Security Incident:   Low - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a limited adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A limited adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is noticeably reduced; (ii) result in minor damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in minor financial loss; or (iv) result in minor harm to individuals   Moderate - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a serious adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A serious adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a significant degradation in mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is able to perform its primary functions, but the effectiveness of the functions is significantly reduced; (ii) result in significant damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in significant financial loss; or (iv) result in significant harm to individuals that does not involve loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   High - The loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability could be expected to have a severe or catastrophic adverse effect on organizational operations, organizational assets, or individuals.  A severe or catastrophic adverse effect means that, for example, the loss of confidentiality, integrity, or availability might: (i) cause a severe degradation in or loss of mission capability to an extent and duration that the organization is not able to perform one or more of its primary functions; (ii) result in major damage to organizational assets; (iii) result in major financial loss; or (iv) result in severe or catastrophic harm to individuals involving loss of life or serious life threatening injuries.   Source:  FIPS 199.  http://csrc.nist.gov/publications/fips/fips199/FIPS-PUB-199-final.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overHeadCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overHeadCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>overHeadCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overheadCostRate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#overheadCostRate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Cost</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>overheadCostRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#owner -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#owner">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>owner</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents an identifier for the owner of the object.  Used and controlled (write-access) by the requesting OS only.  See R_TMF518_FMW_I_0001.This attribute represents an identifier for the owner of the object.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#packetCaptureData -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#packetCaptureData">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SignatureSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>packetCaptureData</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text field to capture PCAP (packet capture) data (i.e. full packets involved in the SecurityEvent)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pagingFileSizeCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pagingFileSizeCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pagingFileSizeCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the current size in amount and units that are stored in the paging files for the Software. If this instance doesn't support paging files, then the value of this attribute should be 0.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#parentCapacity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#parentCapacity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalCapacityDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>parentCapacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a unique name that can be used to identify the PhysicalCapacity that is associated with this ManagedComponent. If this ManagedComponent doesn't contain any other PhysicalCapacities, then the value of this attribute MUST be NULL. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#participationType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#participationType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryParticipation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>participationType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The role that the participant is playing for the associated entry Note: ATTENDEE, ORGANIZER [iCalendar] Permitted Values: ATTENDEE, ORGANIZER, DELEGATED-ATTENDEE, DELEGATED-ORGANIZER</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResourceSpecAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines a manufacturer-allocated part number assigned by the organization that manufactures the hardware item. This, in combination with the ModelNumber and the VendorName, identify different types of hardware items. The SerialNumber can then be used to differentiate between different instances of the same type of hardware item. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyDemographicSource -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyDemographicSource">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyDemographic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyDemographicSource</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The origin of the PartyDemographic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRank -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRank">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdditionalPartyAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyRank</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Degree of importance relative to other partys.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdOfferStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdOfferStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyRoleProdOfferStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The current condition of an PartyRoleProductOffering, such as planned, on-boarded, off-boarded, inactive.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdOffRelType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdOffRelType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProdOffRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyRoleProdOffRelType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as purchase for resell, broker as-is for resale.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdSpecRelType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyRoleProdSpecRelType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProdSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyRoleProdSpecRelType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as purchase for resell, broker as-is for resale.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partySettlementRoleType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partySettlementRoleType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partySettlementRoleType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies the involment such as payment responsible and parties/unit responsible for calculating settlements.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#partyStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdditionalPartyAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>partyStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The current condition of a party, such as active, inactive, prospective.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#passportNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#passportNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PassportIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>passportNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The unique identifier per passport issuer</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#passportType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#passportType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PassportIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>passportType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of Passport. e.g. Personal, Consular</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pattern -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pattern">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SurfaceSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pattern</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A repeated form or design for a surface.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentAcceptedBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentAcceptedBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentAcceptedBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that the associated PartyRole accepts payment for the ProductOffering.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDay -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDay">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PaymentPlan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentDay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The day chosen by the party for generating the payments</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDueDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDueDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OffCyclePartyBill</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentDueDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A party bill payment due date.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDueDateOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentDueDateOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyBillingCycleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentDueDateOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An offset of a payment due date. The offset is expressed as number of days with regard to the start of the BillingPeriod.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentFrequency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentFrequency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayComponentSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentFrequency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>paymentFrequency corresponds to the frequency at which the PayComponentSpecification is applied. For example, it might be applied Monthly for basic pay or Yearly for a Bonus pay component.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentMadeTo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentMadeTo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentMadeTo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies that payment is made to the associated PartyRole for the ProductOffering.  For example, an entrprise may accept payment on behalf of PartyRole and then send the payment to the PartyRole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PaymentPlan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The period of time between two payments.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paymentType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paymentType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paySaleType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#paySaleType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayGrade</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>paySaleType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type associated with the Pay grade scale information based on organisation's pay structure.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pdpCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pdpCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DecisionRequestedDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pdpCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between this ManagedEntity and this PolicyDecisionPoint. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pdpRequestTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pdpRequestTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DecisionRequestedDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pdpRequestTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this ManagedEntity can request decisions of this PolicyDecisionPoint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pepCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pepCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PEPDirectionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pepCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between this PolicyDecisionPoint and this PolicyEnforcementPoint. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pepRequestTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pepRequestTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PEPDirectionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pepRequestTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this PolicyDecisionPoint is allowed to manage this set of PolicyEnforcementPoints.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perceivedSeverity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perceivedSeverity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perceivedSeverity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Lists the possible severities that can be allocated to an Alarm. The values are consistent with ITU-T Recommendation X.733.  Once an alarm has been cleared, its perceived severity is set to Cleared and can no longer be set.   This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#percentage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#percentage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProdOfferPriceAlteration</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>percentage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>percentage specifies the amount of alteration that is applied when it corresponds to a percentage discount, else the price from ComponentProdOfferPrice is used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#percentComplete -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#percentComplete">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SimpleActivity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>percentComplete</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates how much work has been completed for the Activity Permitted Values: 0-100</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlamSpecSeverity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlamSpecSeverity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlamSpecSeverity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value for the  PerceivedSeverity attribute as part of a threshold crossing alarm definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecAdditionalText -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecAdditionalText">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlarmSpecAdditionalText</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value for the  AdditionalText attribute as part of a threshold crossing alarm definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecAlarmType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecAlarmType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlarmSpecAlarmType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value for the AlarmType attribute as part of a threshold crossing alarm definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecProbableCause -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecProbableCause">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlarmSpecProbableCause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value for the ProbableCause attribute as part of a threshold crossing alarm definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecSpecificProblem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmSpecSpecificProblem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlarmSpecSpecificProblem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value for the  SpecificProblem attribute as part of a threshold crossing alarm definition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmThresholdCrossingDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perfAlarmThresholdCrossingDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceAlarmSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perfAlarmThresholdCrossingDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A specific description of the threshold crossing (intended to be populated e under the alarm under CrossedThreshold structure).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#period -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#period">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunicationInteractionItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>period</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CommunicationInteractionItem's period specifies when it happened (starting date and end date).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#periodCoverage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#periodCoverage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AppliedCustomerBillingProductRecurringCharge</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>periodCoverage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The periodCoverage represents the period of time for which this RecurringCharge is being incurred. This period may not be the same as the period covered by the Bill document, for instance due to proration.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perspective -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perspective">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitiveTier</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perspective</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>How the CompetitiveTier is viewed, such as vertical or horizontal.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perspectiveCharacteristic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#perspectiveCharacteristic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitiveTier</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>perspectiveCharacteristic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A feature or quality that further describes the perspective recognizable, such as consumer, business, carrier, size, usage, customer, and so forth. For example, a consumer vertical market perspective.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#photo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#photo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EmployeeIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>photo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A picture or likeness obtained by photography.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalAlarmReportingEnabled -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalAlarmReportingEnabled">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedHardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>physicalAlarmReportingEnabled</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute, and defines whether alarm reporting for this object instance is enabled or not. TRUE means that reporting is allowed, and FALSE means that reporting is inhibited.  Note that some physical entities are not capable of reporting physical alarms, while some are. For those that are not capable of reporting physical alarms, this value MUST be set to FALSE.  Remember that this is for physical alarm reporting. In most cases, there are corresponding logical alarms. The ManagementEntity class hierarchy describes and correlates these.  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalAlarmStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalAlarmStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagedHardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>physicalAlarmStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that indicates the occurrence of an abnormal physical condition relating to an object. This attribute may also function as a summary indicator of alarm conditions associated with a specific resource. It is used to indicate the existence of an alarm condition, a pending alarm condition such as threshold situations, or (when used as a summary indicator) the highest severity of active alarm conditions.  This attribute expands on the standard ITU semantics and updates them to include eTOM concepts. Values include: 0: unknown 1: activeReportable-Critical 2: activeReportable-Major 3: activeReportable-Minor 4: activeReportable-Indeterminate 5: activeReportable-Warning 6: activePendingDecision 7: active-underRepair 8: active-beingReplaced 9: cleared  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalCapacityStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalCapacityStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>physicalCapacityStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer whose value indicates the current status of this category of capacity object. The category is the name of the subclass. For example, the PhysicalMemoryCapacity subclass inherits the Status attribute, so the status applies to this instance of PhysicalMemory. The following values are defined:  0: Unknown 1: OK 2: Initializing 3: Starting 4: Paused 5: Stopping 6: Stopped 7: Degraded 8: Stressed 9: Critical 10: Predicted Failure 11: Error - General 12: Error - Non Recoverable 13: Not Installed or Not Present 14: In Maintenance 15: Unable To Contact 16: Lost Communications  Stopped indicates that the object is known still exist, but it is no longer operational. However, it has not failed. Stressed indicates that the object is functioning, but needs attention (e.g., it may be overheating, or overloaded in some way). Predicted Failure indicates that this object is functioning properly but predicting a failure in the near future.  In Maintenance describes an object that is being configured, maintained, or otherwise administered and is NOT available for service. Unable To Contact indicates that the monitoring system has knowledge of this object but has never been able to establish communications with it. Lost Commmunications indicates that the object has been contacted successfully in the past and is known to still exist; however, it is currently unreachable.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#physicalDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HolderAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>physicalDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that defines the physically unique characteristics of this holder. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pi -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pi">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalOrientation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pi</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The angle between the x axis and the N axis.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pin -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pin">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerBillingAccount</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pin</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A multidigit personal identification number that is used by a Customer to gain access to a BillingAccount at an ATM, a computer, or a telephone system, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pinDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pinDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalConnector</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pinDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string describing the pin configuration and signal usage of a PhysicalConnector.  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#placeOfBirth -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#placeOfBirth">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Individual</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>placeOfBirth</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Note: Pointer to a Location object City, town name etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#placeRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#placeRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductPlaceRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>placeRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Role type of the Place in the context of a Product.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The duration expected during the planning process</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedEnd -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedEnd">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ClosedLoopActivity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedEnd</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Scheduled end of the activity</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedEntryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedEntryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorIntelligenceMarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedEntryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date on which the Competitor intends to begin making ProductOfferings available to a MarketSegment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedMarketCoverage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedMarketCoverage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorIntelligenceMarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedMarketCoverage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A percent or description that describes the degree to which a Competitor will/does/has extend into a MarketSegment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedMarketEntryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedMarketEntryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorMarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedMarketEntryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date on which a Competitor plans to offer ProductOfferings in a MarketSegment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedOrActualCapacity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedOrActualCapacity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Capacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedOrActualCapacity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies whether the capacity is planned or actual.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedOutageIndication -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedOutageIndication">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedOutageIndication</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates that the Managed Object (related to this alarm) is in planned outage (in planned maintenance, or out-of-service). This might also be used when an equipment is being commissioned to avoid the alarms propagating to other systems.  This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedQty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedQty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceReservationAllocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedQty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedSpending -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedSpending">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorIntelligenceMarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedSpending</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount of money that a Competitor intends on spending make ProductOfferings available in a MarketSegment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedStart -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#plannedStart">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ClosedLoopActivity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>plannedStart</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Scheduled start of the activity</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyActionSelectCriteria -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyActionSelectCriteria">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyActionSelectCriteria</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an attribute that contains an OCL expression to prescribe any limitations on the types of PolicyActions that can be used with any PolicyRules that are derived from this particular PolicyRuleSpec. This enables a PolicyRuleSpec to be built that defines what types of PolicyActions can be used to build PolicyRules. This in turn ensures that a given set of PolicyRules carry standard functionality. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyConditionSelectCriteria -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyConditionSelectCriteria">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyConditionSelectCriteria</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an attribute that contains an OCL expression to prescribe any limitations on the types of PolicyConditions that can be used with any PolicyRules that are derived from this particular PolicyRuleSpec. This enables a PolicyRuleSpec to be built that defines what types of PolicyConditions can be used to build PolicyRules. This in turn ensures that a given set of PolicyRules carry standard functionality. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyDomainID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyDomainID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyDomainID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Policy Domain identifier for this capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyEventSelectCriteria -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyEventSelectCriteria">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyEventSelectCriteria</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an attribute that contains an OCL expression to prescribe any limitations on the types of PolicyEvents that can be used with any PolicyRules that are derived from this particular PolicyRuleSpec. This enables a PolicyRuleSpec to be built that defines what types of PolicyEvents can be used to trigger the evaluation of PolicyRules. This in turn ensures that a given set of PolicyRules carry standard functionality. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyGroupID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyGroupID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyGroupID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The policy group identifier for this capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policyName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Policy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policyName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a generic naming attribute that can be used to identify different policy entities. This enables commonName to be used to enforce enterprise or service provider generic naming and this attribute to be used to fine tune the naming of policy entities. Thus, commonName is public in scope and policyName is private to policy.  Notes:   Not present in the ITU specs or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policySetID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#policySetID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>policySetID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the identifier of associated polictSet for this capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#poolAssignmentRestriction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#poolAssignmentRestriction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforcePoolAssignment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>poolAssignmentRestriction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents any limitation of the assignment other than time period. For example, this employee’s assignment to the pool has the highest priority compared to other assignments.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#port -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#port">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityEventEndpoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>port</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The IP port associated with the IP address in the translation</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portabilityStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portabilityStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NumberPortabilityRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>portabilityStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>All the number portability requests have a behavior with an affinity and dependency to the different parties created and added. (NP Clearinghouse, External System, Customer). This relation affects directly to the tracking for the portability through a status. This status is mapped through this attribute called portabilityStatus.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portDirection -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portDirection">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PortVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>portDirection</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines if this variable is used to represent source addresses, destination addresses, or both.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalPort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>portNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a non-zero integer that uniquely identifies this PhysicalPort instance from all other instances. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portRangeEnd -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portRangeEnd">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Protocol</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>portRangeEnd</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This non-negative integer defines the upper range of allowable port numbers to use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portRangeStart -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#portRangeStart">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Protocol</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>portRangeStart</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This non-negative integer defines the lower range of allowable port numbers to use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#positionInChassis -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#positionInChassis">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ChassisPosition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>positionInChassis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is the "slot number" of the Rack that the Chassis is placed in. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#positionNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#positionNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>positionNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The position within the type. Notes: often a number with a suffix, e.g. “5B”</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#possibleDeliveryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#possibleDeliveryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>possibleDeliveryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date upon which the WorkOrder may be completed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#postcode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#postcode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>postcode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A descriptor for a postal delivery area, used to speed and simplify the delivery of mail. Notes: also known as ZIP code</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#postOrderFulfilledBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#postOrderFulfilledBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>postOrderFulfilledBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator the specifies if the party completes fulfillment of an order after it has been taken.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#potentialRootCauseIndication -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#potentialRootCauseIndication">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>potentialRootCauseIndication</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates whether an alarm is a raw (uncorrelated) alarm (when false) or a potential root cause alarm indication (when true).  A fault has typically one root cause, but identifying the true root cause of a fault might be difficult. However, with the scope of an alarm-owning system, it might possible to identify a potential root cause indication that might be useful for client systems.  This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#powerCordNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#powerCordNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Chassis</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>powerCordNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the number of power cords which must be connected to the Chassis in order for all of its contained ManagedEntities to operate correctly. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#powerState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#powerState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>powerState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the current power status of the hardware item. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Not Applicable  2: No Power Applied  3: Full Power Applied  4: Power Save - Normal  5: Power Save - Degraded  6: Power Save - Standby  7: Power Save - Critical  8: Power Save - Low Power Mode  9: Power Save - Unknown  10: Power Cycle  11: Power Warning  12: Power Off  Value 1 means that the hardware item doesn't require the direct application of power (e.g., a but or bolt). If the value for this item is 3, then the PowerCapability class will describe the particular power requirements of this item through the HasPower association.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preceededBy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preceededBy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntityIdentificationSpecFormat</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preceededBy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>One or more characters that precede the EntityIdentification value. For example, the format of a phone number contains dashes, such as 972-477-8401.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#precision -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#precision">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleCurrency</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>precision</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Precision of a currency.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredBundleSpec -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredBundleSpec">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServicePackageBundleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preferredBundleSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains the name of the ServiceBundleSpec that is preferred to be used to implement this particular ServicePackageSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredConfigMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredConfigMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SupportedMgmtMethodDetail</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preferredConfigMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the name of a class that identifies the name of the preferred ManagementMethod for performing configuration operations on the associated ManagedEntity. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: None  2: CLI  3: SNMP  4: TL1  5: CMIP  6: Proprietary  None could mean that this ManagedEntity performs a set function and is not configurable, as well as mean that this ManagedEntity is not configurable except by the factory.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredGivenName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredGivenName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preferredGivenName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains the chosen name by which the person prefers to be addressed. Note: This name may be a name other than a given name, such as a nickname</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredMonitorMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredMonitorMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SupportedMgmtMethodDetail</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preferredMonitorMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the name of a class that identifies the name of the preferred ManagementMethod for performing monitoring operations on the associated ManagedEntity. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: None  2: CLI  3: SNMP  4: RMON  5: CMIP  6: TL1  7: Proprietary  None could mean that this ManagedEntity is not able to be monitored.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredVersionToUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#preferredVersionToUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CFSSpecVersionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>preferredVersionToUse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the preferred Version of this CustomerFacingServiceSpecification to use.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#prescribedAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#prescribedAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecConsequence</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>prescribedAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Recommended remedy for a violated ServiceLevelObjective. A placeholder that indicates an extension may be made to the SID model here to further define remedies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#presizedSIze -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#presizedSIze">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_BacklogItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>presizedSIze</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#price -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#price">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ComponentProdPrice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>price</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount of money that characterizes the price.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priceRuleConditionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priceRuleConditionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProdOfferPriceCondition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>priceRuleConditionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A character string that specifies how to interpret the condition. A value of "Buy" means that the condition specifies how many of an entity must be procured to satisfy the rule. A value of "Price" means that the condition specifies that there is a relationship between prices of two entities that must exist for the condition to be satisfied. The value “ObtainedWithin” specifies dates within which a Product Offering must be procured to satisfy the Policy Condition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priceType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priceType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ComponentProdPrice</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>priceType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A category that describes the price, such as recurring, discount, allowance, penalty, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#principalLocation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#principalLocation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TimeZone</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>principalLocation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priority -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#priority">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>priority</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#privacyType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#privacyType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyPrivacyProfileTypeCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>privacyType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A privacyType specifies the type of Privacy rule specified for an information such as    - “Internal Purpose” : usage of the information by the company that collects the information for a purpose,    - “External Purpose”: usage of the information by the company that received the information from another company for a purpose,    - “Internal Retention”: rights to keep the information for the company that collects the information,    - “External Retention”: rights to keep the information for the company that  that received the information from another company.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#privateStreetName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#privateStreetName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>privateStreetName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Private streets internal to a property (e.g. a university) may have internal names that are not recorded by the land title office.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#probableCause -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#probableCause">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>probableCause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Further qualifies the alarm in complement of the alarmType. This specification does not use an enumeration, but a string with qualified text. Recommended values are specified in TMF063 Probable Causes Technical Specification.  This attribute is mandatory in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#problemEscalation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#problemEscalation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>problemEscalation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if this service problem has been escalated or not. Possible values are 0 to 10. A value of zero means no escalation.  The meanings of values 1-10 are to be determined by the user of the interface, but they show increasing levels of escalation.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#problemId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#problemId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>problemId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifier of the problem. Note that this identifier is local to the server side of the interface.  Only EntityIdentifier can be considered as global.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processesPerUserMax -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processesPerUserMax">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleUsesProcessesDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>processesPerUserMax</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processMemorySizeCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processMemorySizeCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>processMemorySizeCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the amount and units of memory that have been allocated to a Process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#processType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProcessType</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>processType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of process. E.g. ClosedLoop, Workflow, Activity</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#producingApplicationId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#producingApplicationId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MeasurementJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>producingApplicationId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The identifier of the application that consumes performance indicators.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#productionReason -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#productionReason">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyBillingCycle</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>productionReason</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The reason for this cycle run. Values may be SCHEDULE_RUN, PROVEIDER_REQUEST or others</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#programDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#programDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NumberPortabilityRequest</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>programDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute called programDate is used to program the date to port (hence the name) for Port In and Port Out of the portability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#projectNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#projectNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>projectNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique identifier for the Project</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#proposedRepairActions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#proposedRepairActions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>proposedRepairActions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates proposed repair actions, if known to the system emitting the alarm.  This attribute is optional in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#proseFormula -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#proseFormula">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionDeterminationMethod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>proseFormula</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A prose expression of formula, may not be as precise as the XLS formula or some XLS-like formula.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protectionRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protectionRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>protectionRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the protection role that this equipment plays. In case the equipment is not protected, the value "NOT_APPLICABLE" shall be used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protectionSchemeState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protectionSchemeState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>protectionSchemeState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute identifies the individual lock of this equipment. In case the equipment is not protected, the value "UNKNOWN" shall also be used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protocol -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protocol">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetFlowSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>protocol</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Integer number of the protocol used in the network flow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protocolDirection -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#protocolDirection">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Protocol</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>protocolDirection</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the direction of this protocol. Values are:  0: input  1: output  2: bi-directional</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#provessValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#provessValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>provessValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the value to be assigned to the process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#psi -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#psi">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalOrientation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>psi</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The angle between the N axis and the X axis.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#publishedDateTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#publishedDateTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>publishedDateTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date and time the vulnerability was published to the public.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purchaseOrderNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purchaseOrderNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>purchaseOrderNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that uniquely identifies a ProductOrder within the ordering Party's enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purpose -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purpose">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRoleProductOffering</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>purpose</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The reason for the PartyRoleProductOffering, such as sell on behalf of, purchase, offer.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purposeDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#purposeDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Slot</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>purposeDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that defines the physically unique characteristics of this Slot. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpActionCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpActionCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionPerformedDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpActionCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between this ManagedEntity and this PolicyExecutionPoint. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpAllowedActionTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpAllowedActionTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyActionPerformedDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpAllowedActionTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this PolicyExecutionPoint can perform actions on this ManagedEntity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PXPDirectionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between this PolicyDecisionPoint and this PolicyExecutionPoint. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpEnforcementCommMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpEnforcementCommMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PXPEnforcementDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpEnforcementCommMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the communication method used between this PolicyExecutionPoint and this PolicyEnforcementPoint. Values include: 0: Not yet established 1: Telnet 2: COPS 3: Proprietary Protocol</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpEnforcementRequestTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpEnforcementRequestTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PXPEnforcementDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpEnforcementRequestTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this PolicyEnforcementPoint must enforce the actions taken by this PolicyExecutionPoint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpRequestTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#pxpRequestTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PXPDirectionDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>pxpRequestTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the start and end times (in the form of time stamps) in which this PolicyDecisionPoint is allowed to manage this set of PolicyExecutionPoints.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#qty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#qty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductSpecActivitySpecAllocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>qty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#qualifications -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#qualifications">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IndividualName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>qualifications</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains the letters used to describe academic or other type qualifications held by a person and/or the distinctions conferred upon them. e.g. PhD, MD, CPA, MCSD, etc Note: also known as orders, decorations, honors, awards and distinctions</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#quantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#quantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AppliedCustomerBillingRate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>quantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unit (for example, US Dollars) and number of the applied rate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#quantityRangeInterval -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#quantityRangeInterval">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevShareModelSpecNegotiableRange</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>quantityRangeInterval</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies the inclusion or exclusion of the lower range and upper range quantity attributes. Possible values are "open", "closed", "closedBottom" and "closedTop".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#raAssessmentType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#raAssessmentType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevenueAssuranceAssessment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>raAssessmentType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A category that groups assessments that have strongly marked and readily defined similarities. For example, effectiveness, trend analysis, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rangeInterval -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rangeInterval">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristicValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rangeInterval</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies the inclusion or exclusion of the valueFrom and valueTo attributes.  Possible values are "open", "closed", "closedBottom" and "closedTop".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rangeStep -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rangeStep">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CharacteristicSpecValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rangeStep</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The specification that a range of values increases in steps, such as a range from 0 to 100 in steps of 5 with the resulting permitted values being 0, 5, 10, 15,...100. This complements the valueFrom, valueTo, and rangeInterval attributes. Previously there was no way to do so, and individual CharacteristicSpecValues had to be created.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rank -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rank">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitorMarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rank</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The degree of importance or excellence of a Competitor in a MarketSegment relative to other Competitors in the MarketSegment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SimpleRateTaxDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The percentage rate for calculating the tax. For example, 17% for value added tax.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#readingProficiency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#readingProficiency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LanguageAbility</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>readingProficiency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Degree of mastery in reading a language.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reason -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reason">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reason</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that describes the reason for creating this version.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reconciliationDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reconciliationDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevenueShareReconciliation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reconciliationDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date that a PartyRevenueShare was reconciled.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reconciliationDateComplete -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reconciliationDateComplete">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevenueShareReconciliation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reconciliationDateComplete</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date that a PartyRevenueShareReconciliation is completed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#recorderInfo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#recorderInfo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRDoc</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>recorderInfo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#recurringFrequency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#recurringFrequency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RecurringScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>recurringFrequency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A recurring frequency to run a job within day that is included in schedule definition, for example: every 5 minutes, 15 minuute, 30 minutes, 1 hour.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#redundancy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#redundancy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>redundancy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that describes the redundancy capabilities of this particular Equipment. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Primary (supported by a Redundant Equipment)  2: Redundant (supports a Primary Equipment)  3: Stand-alone (no Redundancy possible)  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reference -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reference">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityThreatActor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reference</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A reference to additional information about a threat.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relatedEntity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relatedEntity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Anomaly</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relatedEntity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>related entity identifier where this anomaly is applicable</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipReason -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipReason">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relationshipReason</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that explains the reason for the association between the SoftwareResourceSpecifications.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductFinancialAccountRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relationshipType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A categorization of the relationship, such as aggregation, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipTypeCode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relationshipTypeCode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relationshipTypeCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An enumeration of the values for a particular type of SoftwareSpecificationRelationship that is dependent on the relationshipType attribute.  For example, for a Refinement type of relationship the value may represent a substitution, division, or fusion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relativeElevation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relativeElevation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NetworkRouteSection</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relativeElevation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The relative height to which something is elevated above a point of reference such as the ground.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relativeModifier -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relativeModifier">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PlacePartyRoleAssoc</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relativeModifier</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>If the association is relative to the location (not at it) then use a modifier NEAR-TO or OUTSIDE or ACROSS-ROAD-FROM ?.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#releaseStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#releaseStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResourceSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>releaseStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that defines the particualr release status of this SoftwareResourceSpecification. Values include: 0: alpha 1. beta 2: FCS (First Customer Shipment) 3. GD (General Deployment) 4: SV (Special Version for 1 or more customers) 5: EOE (end of engineering) 6: EOS (end of sale) 7: EOL (end of life) FCS marks the beginning of the limited deployment phase. In this phase, the SoftwareResourceSpecification is usually certified on a few platforms but not all platforms. GD marks the certification of stable SoftwareResourceSpecification on all major platforms. SV is a special build for a particular customer that needs special fixes or features. EOE means that no new engineering fixes will be applied, but the SoftwareResourceSpecification can still be ordered. EOS means that the SoftwareResourceSpecificatino can no longer be ordered, but will still be supported. EOL means that the SofwareResourceSpecification can no longer be supported, and cannot be ordered.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#relType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>relType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies the relationship type of two PartySettlements suh as migration, substitution, dependency, exclusivity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#remainingAmount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#remainingAmount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AccountBalance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>remainingAmount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Remained or owed account balance amount. Here Quantity type represents both non-monetary balance and monetary balance. Non-monetary balance is applied to the service usage volume and monetary balance is applied to the monetary amount.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#remainingValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#remainingValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UsageVolumeBalance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>remainingValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The remainingValue is a calculated value based on UsageVolumeBalanceCredits and UsageVolumeBalanceDebits.  When the remainingValue is 0, no more UsageVolumeBalanceDebit can be decremented from the Balance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#removable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#removable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalContainer</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>removable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean that defines whether it is possible to insert and remove this object instance from the Equipment in which it is installed, without impairing the function or packaging of the Equipment. TRUE means that it is removable, and FALSE means that it is not.  A Package can still be Removable if power must be 'off' in order to perform the removal. If power can be 'on' and this object instance can still be removed, then this object instance is both Removable and HotSwappable.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reorderLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reorderLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemStockLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reorderLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Quantity under wich StockItem must be reordered (only for type = Available for Sale or Use).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reorderQuantity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reorderQuantity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemStockLevel</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reorderQuantity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Quantity of StockItem that must be reordered when quantity is under reorderLevel (only for type = Available for Sale or Use)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#repeatAction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#repeatAction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyConsequence</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>repeatAction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Recommended repeatAction when a qualifying condition is met</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#repeatCount -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#repeatCount">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>repeatCount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The number of times the alarm should be repeated, after the initial trigger [iCalendar] Notes: REPEAT [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#replaceable -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#replaceable">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalContainer</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>replaceable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean that defines whether it is possible to replace this object instance with a physically different instance of the same type. For example, some types of device allow various Chips to be upgraded. TRUE means that it is replaceable, and FALSE means that it is not.  All Removable packages are inherently Replaceable.  This is a required attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#replacementDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#replacementDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElementRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>replacementDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date that the substitution, division or fusion takes effect.  Only applicable if type is Replacement.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportingPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportingPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MeasurementCollectionJob</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reportingPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The rate of collecting Performance Indicators reports.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportSequenceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportSequenceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IntentReport</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reportSequenceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies the sequence number of intent reports sent to owner.  Individual intents may have a sequence of reports directly related to this intent.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportTimeStamp -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportTimeStamp">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyReport</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reportTimeStamp</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date and time from when the information is  captured in the AnomalyReport </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportTimestamp -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reportTimestamp">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IntentReport</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reportTimestamp</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The timestamp of when the intent handler created the intent report.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedCompletionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedCompletionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestedCompletionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Requested delivery date from the requestor perspective.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemShipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestedDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date on which the StockItemShipment should be completed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedDeliveryDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedDeliveryDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestedDeliveryDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date upon which the WorkOrder is desired to be completed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedParticipation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedParticipation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryParticipation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestedParticipation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The requested participation status Note: ROLE [iCalendar] Permitted Values: REQ-PARTICIPANT, OPT-PARTICIPANT, NON-PARTICIPANT</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedStartDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestedStartDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProductOrder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestedStartDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Order fulfillment start date wished by the requestor. This is used when, for any reason, requestor cannot allow seller to begin to operationally begin the fulfillment before a date. It can happen for example in the context of a move.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryParticipation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates if the request has been delivered to the participant and if it has been read (but not actioned) Permitted Value: DELIVERED-UNREAD, READ, UNDELIVERED</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requestType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StockItemRequest</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requestType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The requestType might be          • Booking request: a booking request might come from a CustomerOrder in progress or simply from a salesperson that plan to place a huge quantity to a Customer. It carries a valid period to avoid freezing the stock.          • Replenishment: a replenishment request is triggered when the quantity is under the reorderLevel.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requirements -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requirements">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requirements</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that defines the recommend power supply configuration required as a function of how populated the Equipment is. Often in networking devices, higher-capacity power supplies must be used in place of lower-capacity ones when the type and/or number of installed Cards exceeds a certain number. In addition, in order to have fully-redundant power, higher-capacity power supplies must sometimes be used, again depending on the type and number of Cards installed. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requisiteSkillSet -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#requisiteSkillSet">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceRolePartyRoleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>requisiteSkillSet</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an array of integers, and is used to define a set of skills that are required for this PartyRole to possess in order to manage this Resource. The values appear as a comma separated list.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reservedFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#reservedFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceAllocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>reservedFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resolutionTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resolutionTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_Impediment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resolutionTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceAccess -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceAccess">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyAppliesToDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourceAccess</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the access privileges that the resource has. This may restrict the performance of operations that a user (human or otherwise) has access to when performing various operations on a ManagedEntity residing in a specific PolicyDomain.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceFulfillmentState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceFulfillmentState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Equipment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourceFulfillmentState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute supports basic administration of plug-ins.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourcePolicyValidFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourcePolicyValidFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceManagementPolicy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourcePolicyValidFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a period of time that this particular ResourcePolicy is valid for. A TimePeriod is a complex datatype that contains both a starting and ending time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceRate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceRate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourceRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resources -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resources">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarActionEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resources</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The equipment or resource requirements Note: RESOURCES [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonResourceInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourceState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>See R_TMF518_NRB_I_0001.   See SD2-17_EnhancedResourceStates supporting document...\SD\SD2-17_EnhancedResourceStates.pdf</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#resourceUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RunningSoftwareStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>resourceUse</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The quantity (amount, units) of a Resource being used by Software.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#respectsThreshold -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#respectsThreshold">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Segment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>respectsThreshold</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The attribute respectsThreshold specifies if the Segment respects the lower and upper size defined by the SegmentSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#respondedParticipation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#respondedParticipation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntryParticipation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>respondedParticipation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The responded participation status Note PARTSTAT [iCalendar] Permitted Values: refer [iCalendar]</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#responseTypeFormat -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#responseTypeFormat">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>APISpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>responseTypeFormat</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Response type format of this API like Text and Json.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#responsibleParty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#responsibleParty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Problem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>responsibleParty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Person or organization responsible for handling this problem. This is text or structured text and not an association to a party object. The Who category from the ATIS Service Outage document can be used for this attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retrievalMethodCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retrievalMethodCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>retrievalMethodCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the particular type of method that is currently being used to retrieve the management information. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: None  2: CLI  3: SNMP  4: TL1  5: CMIP  6: RMON  7: Proprietary  None could mean that this ManagedEntity performs a set function and is not configurable, as well as mean that this ManagedEntity is not configurable except by the factory.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retrievalMethodsSupported -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retrievalMethodsSupported">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ManagementInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>retrievalMethodsSupported</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of integers that define the different means of retrieving management methods that are supported by this object. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: None  2: CLI  3: SNMP  4: TL1  5: CMIP  6: RMON  7: Proprietary  None could mean that this ManagedEntity performs a set function and is not configurable, as well as mean that this ManagedEntity is not configurable except by the factory.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retryNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retryNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventTriggerDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>retryNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This specifies the number of times that this PolicyEvent should be resent to the specified PolicyRule. If the triggerEndTime elapses, then this PolicyEvent will not be resent anymore, even if the retryNumber indicates that additional retries should be attempted. Instead, the hasEventEvaluated attribute of this PolicyEvent must be set to 2 (failed to be evaluated).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retryPolicy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#retryPolicy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventTriggerDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>retryPolicy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the policy for retrying triggers. An enumeration enables the policy application to choose among a set of pre-defined policies for determining how many times to retry sending this PolicyEvent to its associated PolicyRule. Values include: 0 - do NOT retry 1 - always retry (until successful acknowledgment) 2 - retry the number of times specified in the retryNumber attribute</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueCode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueCode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AppliedCustomerBillingRateSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revenueCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The revenue type represented by this AppliedCustomerBillingRateSpec. This attribute has at least 3 valid values:  RC - (for recurring charge)  UC - (for usage charge)  OC - (for one-time charge)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueShareProvidedUsing -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueShareProvidedUsing">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevShareTermOrCondition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revenueShareProvidedUsing</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Specifies how the revenue sharing information is provided. For example, on a revenue sharing notice, bill/invoice, or payment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueShareTimePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revenueShareTimePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRevShareTermOrCondition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revenueShareTimePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time period for which revenue shares should be determined. For example, weekly, monthly, quarterly.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revisionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date the version was created.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revisionNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents the occurrence of the version in the sequence of versions. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#revisionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>revisionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The significance of the revision.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rfsStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rfsStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceFacingService</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rfsStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the status of this particular ResourceFacingService. Values include: 0: Operational and supporting CFS 1: Degraded but supporting CFS 2: In Violation and not supporting CFS 3: Operational but not yet supporting a CFS 4: Being Tested 5: Being Deployed 6: Failed Value 0 means that this ResourceFacingService is acting per specification, and is also currently supporting one or more CustomerFacingServices. Value 1 means that this ResourceFacingService is operational, but is currently in a degraded state. This degraded state indicates congestion or some other problem, but has not yet comprimised the operation of its associated CustomerFacingServices. Value 2 means that this ResourceFacingService is operational, but is currently in violation of its associated specification(s). This in turn means that its associated CustomerFacingServices are violating their contractual specification(s) unless automatic fail-over has been enabled. Value 3 means that this ResourceFacingService is acting per specification, but is not yet currently supporting one or more CustomerFacingServices. Value 4 means that this ResourceFacingService is currently being tested, and is not yet ready to support a CustomerFacingService. Value 5 means that this ResourceFacingService is currently being deployed, and is not yet ready to support a CustomerFacingService. Value 6 means that this ResourceFacingService has currently failed. The set of actions that should be taken, as well as whether this service can still be billed or not, are determined by its associated Policy for handling service violations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#role -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#role">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentRelatedParty</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>role</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Enumeration of the roles the Security Party plays in the incident, such as Notifying, Affected, Tracking.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleCombination -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleCombination">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Role</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>roleCombination</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A roleCombination is an array of string attributes that are used to identify and potentially select one or more policies for a set of managed entities from among a much larger set of available policies. Values of this attribute should be entered in comma separated value format; white space should be ignored.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssociationRoleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>roleName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Text that provides the name of the role a RootEntityType plays in an association.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleNbr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleNbr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssociationRoleSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>roleNbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number assigned to a RootEntityType's involvement in an association. Valid values are 1 or 2, because this model only supports binary associations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleSelectionMethod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleSelectionMethod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Role</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>roleSelectionMethod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the precise means used to select one or more entities which map to one or more roles contained in the roleCombination attribute of this object. Values include: 0: retrieve all 1: retrieve intersection For exampe, assume that there is an external query engine that is looking for the roles edge or ethernet. The result of this query will look at the roleCombination and roleSelectionMethod attributes of each managed object that it is querying. If the value of this attribute is 0, then all managed objects that have their roleCombination set to either {edge}, {ethernet}, or {edge, ethernet} will be retrieved. In contrast, if the value of this attribute is 1, then only those managed objects whose roleCombination attribute is set to {edge, ethernet} will be retrieved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#roleType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceSpecificationPerfRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>roleType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A function that a ResourceSpecification plays in defining a PerformanceSpecification, such as source, destination, related, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rootCause -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#rootCause">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentAttackMethod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>rootCause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Description of the root cause of the attack</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#routeGroupLabel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#routeGroupLabel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreControlPlane</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>routeGroupLabel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents the Route Group the FRE is associated to. When a target OS creates a Call with diverse Route Groups, it assigns a Route Group label (which may be a number) to each FRE. FREs in the same Route Group will be assigned the same value for routeGroupLabel. FREs in different Route Groups will be assigned different values for routeGroupLabel.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#routingConstraintEffort -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#routingConstraintEffort">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FreControlPlane</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>routingConstraintEffort</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates the requested level of effort to meet the routing constraint when creating and when rerouting the FRE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scalarValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scalarValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionMethodArgument</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scalarValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A quantity that can assume any of a set of values.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A scan of the identification paper Note: May be used to get a copy of the photo to help in identification</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledDates -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledDates">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DateScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduledDates</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The list of dates  when the date schedule definition is active on, e.g.November 1st 2022.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduledDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The duration expected during the detailed scheduling process</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionEndTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionEndTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RecurringScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduleDefinitionEndTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Endtime of the Schedule Definition. If the attribute is empty the Schedule run forever, not having a time constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionHoursRange -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionHoursRange">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RecurringScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduleDefinitionHoursRange</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of time ranges within a specific day that the schedule will be active on, for example 08:00-12:00, 16:00-19:00.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionStartTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleDefinitionStartTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RecurringScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduleDefinitionStartTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Start time of the Schedule Definition. If the attribute is empty the Schedule will be active immediately.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledQty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduledQty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceReservationAllocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduledQty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleStartOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scheduleStartOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RecurringScheduleDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scheduleStartOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an offeset relating  to the recurring interval. For example, if the recurring interval is 1 hour and the offset is 10 minutes, a job will be executed at 1:10, 2:10, 3:10, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#schemaName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#schemaName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TemplateBlock</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>schemaName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scoringSequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#scoringSequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>scoringSequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The order in which the score for the metric is calculated.  This ensures that a metric's score upon which another is dependent is calculated first.   Notes:  For example, the Base Exploitability Score is calculated after the Access Vector, Authentication, and Access Complexity scores are calculated.  Also, the Base Score has to be calculated from the Base Metrics before scoring the Temporal and/or Environmental Metrics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sdStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sdStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceDefinition</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sdStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The state of the Service Definition; it may take on one of the following values: Draft, Standard, or Proprietary.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#securityBreach -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#securityBreach">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>securityBreach</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated 16-bit unsigned integer attribute indicating whether a breach of the Rack was attempted. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Other  2: No Breach  3: Unsuccessful Breach (but attempted)  4: Successful Breach  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#securityBreachDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#securityBreachDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>securityBreachDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string attribute that provides supplementary information for the SecurityBreach attribute. It should only be filled in when the value of SecurityBreach is 1 ("Other").  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#semantics -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#semantics">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>semantics</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that is used to define the particular semantics of this version. This string should include as a minimum a description of the format of the revisionNumber.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#seqNum -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#seqNum">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MatrixCharValueIndex</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>seqNum</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Holds the sequentialnumber of the dimension that this index applies to</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommunicationInteractionItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The CommunicationInteractionItem’s sequence specifies the order in which they follow one another.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequencedActions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequencedActions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicyRuleSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sequencedActions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer defines how the ordering of the PolicyActions associated with this PolicyRule is to be interpreted.  Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs (the CIM defined a subset of these values as an attribute in the PolicyRule).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceNum -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceNum">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Anomaly</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sequenceNum</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique sequence of Anomaly used to identify the Anomaly management session</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PayGrade</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sequenceNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The sequence maintained at the pay scale type for the same pay grade to maintain the differences in the payment amount in the payroll system.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceOfApplication -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sequenceOfApplication">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureThresholdConsequence</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sequenceOfApplication</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents the sequence in which a MetricDefMeasureConsequence should be applied for a MetricDefMeasureThresholdRule.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serialNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serialNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serialNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A set of identifying characters and/or numbers assigned to, and usually marked on, each of a series of identical Software instances.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceAffecting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceAffecting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceAffecting</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Provides the alarm-owning system determination of whether or not the alarm affects service.    This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceApproach -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceApproach">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HolderComposite</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceApproach</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated, integer-valued array that defines how this entity is serviced (e.g., from the top or front), whether it has sliding trays or removable sides, and/or whether the Frame is moveable (e.g., it has rollers). Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Custom  2: Service From Top  3: Service From Front  4: Service From Back  5: Service From Side  6: Sliding Trays  7: Removable Sides  8: Moveable  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelObjective -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelObjective">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceLevelObjective</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a ServiceLevelSpecObjective is part of the expresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecApplicability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecApplicability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceLevelSpecApplicability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a ServiceLevelSpecApplicability is part of the expresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecConsequence -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecConsequence">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceLevelSpecConsequence</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a ServiceLevelSpecConsequence is part of the expresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecParameter -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLevelSpecParameter">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecExpression</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceLevelSpecParameter</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that is set to true if a ServiceLevelSpecParameter is part of the expresssion.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLocation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceLocation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceTemplate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceLocation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Gives the URL of where the service component activation OS is actually located.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#servicePolicyValidFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#servicePolicyValidFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceManagementPolicy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>servicePolicyValidFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a period of time that this particular ServicePolicy is valid for. A TimePeriod is a complex datatype that contains both a starting and ending time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceRestoredDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceRestoredDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceRestoredDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date on which the service was brought back to its original condition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#serviceState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceAccessPoint</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>serviceState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the ability of an entity to provide service.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sessionID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sessionID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sessionID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sessionTerminationCause -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sessionTerminationCause">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PublicWANAccessUsageEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sessionTerminationCause</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#settlementDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#settlementDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>settlementDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Issue date of a PartySettlement.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#settlementNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#settlementNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>settlementNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique identifier that enables different instances of a PartySettlement to be distinguished from each other.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#severity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#severity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerProblem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>severity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The severity of the CustomerProblem (in the eyes of the CSP).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sharedRiskGroupList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sharedRiskGroupList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RoutingParameters</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sharedRiskGroupList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute specifies the shared risk that in general is considered against the physical environment. It is defined as a sequence of {risk type, and sequence of shared risk references (strings)}.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sharedSlots -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sharedSlots">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdjacentSlotDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sharedSlots</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that if this Slot (i.e., Slot n) is populated by an adapter Card, then the next Slot (i.e., Slot n+1) must be left empty. This is because Slots can often be located in close proximity, such that if one of these Slots is occupied, there is no room to access the next Slot. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#signatureRepresentation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#signatureRepresentation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AgreementAuthorization</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>signatureRepresentation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indication that represents whether the signature is a physical paper signature or a digital signature.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#size -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#size">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CompetitiveTier</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>size</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>How big the Competitor is, such as small, medium, large, compared to other Competitors.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skillLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skillLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkforceEmployeeRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>skillLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the qualification level of the technician: for example, intern, entry level, senior/highly qualified</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skills -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skills">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>skills</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skuNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#skuNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResourceSpecAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>skuNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the manufacturer-allocated Stock Keeping Unit (SKU) number of the hardware item. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slaName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slaName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssuranceCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slaName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The name of corresponding Service Level Agreement for this capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotLayout -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotLayout">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotLayout</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that describes the positioning, spacing, typical usage, restrictions, and any other pertinent information that defines how the Card is to be positioned into the Slot.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CardOnCardDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a number defining the SlotNumber of the hosting Card that this DaughterCard plugs into. If there is no such SlotNumber, then this value should be set to 0. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotPurpose -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotPurpose">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Slot</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotPurpose</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the purpose of this Slot. A specific value below, such as System, means that the Slot is intended only to accept System cards. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: System  2: Networking  3: Port Adapter  4: Memory  5: Hardware Assist  6: Video  7: General Computing  8: General Purpose  Hardware assist is a generic category for specialty boards that provide hardware functionality to assist in the processing of one or more functions. Examples are special cards for processing IPsec-based encryption.  General computing boards represent cards that have additional and/or auxiliary computing power that can be used for a variety of tasks (not just video rendering or encryption).  General purpose boards represent cards that have a variety of features (e.g., memory and computing).  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotSpacingMax -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotSpacingMax">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdjacentSlotDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotSpacingMax</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a 16-bit unsigned integer attribute that indicates the maximum spacing between slots in inches. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotSpacingMin -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotSpacingMin">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AdjacentSlotDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotSpacingMin</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a 16-bit unsigned integer attribute that indicates the minimum spacing between slots in inches. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotsRequired -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slotsRequired">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slotsRequired</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an integer that defines the number of slots required to hold this Card. Since this is usually 1, that value is assigned as its default value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slsID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#slsID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AssuranceCapabilitySpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>slsID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The identifier of corresponding Service Level specification which determines assurance parameters for this capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#socialSecurityNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#socialSecurityNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SocialSecurityNrIdentification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>socialSecurityNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A nine-digit number issued to U.S. citizens, permanent residents, and temporary (working) residents.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#softwareVersionMinReq -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#softwareVersionMinReq">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceSpecRunsSoftwareSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>softwareVersionMinReq</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the minimum version of the Software that is required for this ResourceSpecification to act properly.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#source -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#source">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceTemplate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>source</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Determines whether the source of the OS providing the Service Template is “external” or “internal” to a given organization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sourcedAssets -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#sourcedAssets">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Community</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>sourcedAssets</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Number of assets sourced from the Community</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#speakingProficiency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#speakingProficiency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LanguageAbility</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>speakingProficiency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Degree of mastery in speaking a language.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specificProblem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specificProblem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>specificProblem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Further qualifies the alarm in addition to the probableCause. This attribute is defined as a string. Values are defined by vendors.   This attribute is optional in all 3 profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartySettlementSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>specType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A classification that groups PartySettlemenSpecifications that share common characteristics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specVersionNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#specVersionNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ActivitySpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>specVersionNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#staffHoursLost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#staffHoursLost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentImpact</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>staffHoursLost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Estimate of staff hours lost due to the incident</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardCapacityRequired -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardCapacityRequired">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>standardCapacityRequired</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Standard workforce capacity (man hour, man day) under normal condition and assumptions that the work requires to be completed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardDrivingTime -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardDrivingTime">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkSpecFulfillmentRate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>standardDrivingTime</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Standard driving time for the organization’s technicians to drive to and between work places in the serving area</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#standardDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>standardDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Standard duration of time, under normal condition and assumptions, that the work can take to be completed</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startActivty -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startActivty">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>startActivty</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents the action that triggers the workflow. Linked to Activity ABE. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BusinessInteraction</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>startDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Date interaction initiated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>startEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the event signaling start of the workflow.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startingDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startingDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DunningCase</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>startingDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>As soon as an event triggering a DunningRule occurs on a BillingAccount, a DunningCase is created according to the DunningScenario assigned to the BillingAccount. This date corresponds to the startingDate</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startMode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#startMode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Service</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>startMode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that indicates how the Service is started. Values include: 0: Unknown 1: Automatically by the managed environment 2: Automatically by the owning device 3: Manually by the Provider of the Service 4: Manually by a Customer of the Provider 5: Any of the above</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#state -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#state">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Test</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>state</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The actual state the test is in</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statementOfIntent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statementOfIntent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Agreement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>statementOfIntent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An overview and goals of the Agreement.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#stateOrProvince -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#stateOrProvince">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>GeographicAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>stateOrProvince</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The state or province that the address is in. Synonyms / Aliases: province, territory</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statisticForPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statisticForPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CustomerBillingStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>statisticForPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The period for which the statistic is calculated.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#status -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#status">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>status</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Used to track the lifecycle status, e.g. existing, prospective or former customers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statusEffectiveDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#statusEffectiveDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AgreementAuthorization</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>statusEffectiveDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date associated with the status.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The name of the street or other street type.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNamePrefix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNamePrefix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AmericanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNamePrefix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A word, letter, or number placed before the street name.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNameSuffix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNameSuffix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AmericanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNameSuffix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A word, letter, or number placed after the street name.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirst -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirst">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrFirst</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number identifying a specific property on a public street. It may be combined with streetNrLast for ranged addresses. Notes: A ranged address could be “26-28 XXX Street”</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirstPrefix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirstPrefix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AmericanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrFirstPrefix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A word, letter, or number placed before the street number.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirstSuffix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrFirstSuffix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrFirstSuffix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The first street number suffix. Notes: e.g. “A” for address “101A”</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLast -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLast">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrLast</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The last number in a range of street numbers allocated to a property. Notes: only entered for ranged addresses, otherwise left blank</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLastPrefix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLastPrefix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AmericanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrLastPrefix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A word, letter, or number placed before last number in a range of street numbers allocated to a property.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLastSuffix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetNrLastSuffix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetNrLastSuffix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The last street number suffix for a ranged address.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetSuffix -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetSuffix">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertyAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetSuffix</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A modifier denoting a relative direction Notes: e.g. CENTRAL, EAST, LOWER, NORTH, NORTH EAST, NORTH WEST, SOUTH, SOUTH EAST, SOUTH WEST, UPPER, WEST</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#streetType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StreetName</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>streetType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The kind of street, such as alley, avenue, boulevard, brae, crescent, drive, highway, lane, terrace, parade, place, tarn, way, wharf. Notes: may need to store a set of abbreviations as well</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#stStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#stStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceTemplate</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>stStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The state of the Service Template; it may take on one of the following values: Draft, Pilot, Commercial, Retired.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subCategory -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subCategory">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subCategory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A further classification of MarketSegments because they share common characteristics. For example, a vertical category MarketSegment may be further categorized as consumer, business, or carrier.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subnetMask -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subnetMask">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subnetMask</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the subnet mask for the IP Address of this instance. The IP Address is constructed by concatenating the networkNumber and the hostNumber, forming a dotted decimal IP Address. The subnetMask is formatted according to the appropriate convention as defined in the addressFormat attribute of this object.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WorkflowType</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents additional information that identify the secondary workflow types associated to a primary type.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subtype -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subtype">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ClosedLoopExitBy</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subtype</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A sub-category of an end trigger. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subUnitNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subUnitNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subUnitNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The discriminator used for the subunit. Notes: often just a sumple number e.g. FLAT 5, may also be a range</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subUnitType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#subUnitType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UrbanPropertySubAddress</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>subUnitType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of subunit. Notes: e.g.BERTH, FLAT, PIER, SUITE, SHOP, TOWER, UNIT, WHARF</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#suburb -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#suburb">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StreetSegment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>suburb</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An outlying district of a city, especially a residential one.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#summary -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#summary">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CalendarEntry</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>summary</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A summarized description or subject of the entry</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#supportedMgmtMethods -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#supportedMgmtMethods">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SupportedMgmtMethodDetail</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>supportedMgmtMethods</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an array of strings. Each string contains the name of a class that identifies the name of a supported ManagementMethod for this class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#swapSpaceUsedCurrent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#swapSpaceUsedCurrent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>InstalledSoftware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>swapSpaceUsedCurrent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This defines the current swap space in amount and units that is being used. If the Software doesn't distinguish swap space from space used for paging files, then the value of this attribute should be 0.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#swotType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#swotType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SWOT</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>swotType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A category of organizational analysis, such as strength (S), weakness (W), opportunity (O), threat (T).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbol -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbol">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Currency</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>symbol</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Symbol of a currency, such as $.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbolName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbolName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PointSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>symbolName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A word, term, or phrase by which a PointSymbology is known and distinguished from other PointSymbologys.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbolSize -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#symbolSize">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PointSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>symbolSize</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>How big the PointSymbology is.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#synopsis -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#synopsis">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>synopsis</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Free text synopsis for analyst notes</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#systemDN -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#systemDN">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>systemDN</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the alarm-owning system, i.e. the one owning the alarm list.   This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile, optional in the Standard profile and mandatory in the Enhanced profile.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#systemID -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#systemID">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ExternalSystemCapability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>systemID</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Unique system identifier providing the capability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetNetwork -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetNetwork">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NACSecurityEvent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>targetNetwork</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>URI-based name of the network the subject attempted to gain access to.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetPlatform -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetPlatform">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SoftwareResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>targetPlatform</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the target platform that the SoftwareResource will be deployed on. Values include:  0: Independent of Platform  1: Other  2: Network Device (specified in subclasses)  3: Server  4: Desktop Computer  5: Laptop Computer  6: PDA  7: Phone  8: Other Mobile Device</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetUsedAs -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#targetUsedAs">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncident</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>targetUsedAs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Description of the how the compromised resource was used by the attacker.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#taskFunctionalArea -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#taskFunctionalArea">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_Task</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>taskFunctionalArea</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#technicalDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#technicalDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>technicalDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Details on the technical characteristics of the vulnerability</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#telephonyType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#telephonyType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>NumberPortabilityRequest</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>telephonyType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>It considers the type of telephony for numbers for the portability, like mobile, fixed and IP numbers related to the request.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#templateId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#templateId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPDRSPData</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>templateId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#texture -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#texture">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SurfaceSymbology</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>texture</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The feel, appearance, or consistency of a surface.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#theta -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#theta">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalOrientation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>theta</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The angle between the z axis and the Z axis</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thirdPartyType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thirdPartyType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ThirdPartyCollectionPM</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thirdPartyType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A classification of  the third party which collects the money for service provider, such as bank transfer, payment tool.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdCrossingDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdCrossingDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdCrossingDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Contains further information on the threshold crossing alarm. Vendors should avoid using this field to put additional information identifying the indicator or the threshold id. The corresponding fields should be use for better alarm quality.  For complex thresholds involving multiple indicators, this field is required to provide a textual description of the threshold crossing condition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the identifier of the threshold that caused the alarm.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdParams -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdParams">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceThresholdRulePreDefinedParam</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdParams</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A name-value pair representing a predefined threshold parameters.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdQualifier -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdQualifier">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CrossedThreshold</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdQualifier</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute contains a set of name/ value pairs used to qualify the crossed threshold.   When migrating from MTOSI, this attribute can contain the pmLocation and the thresholdType.   For pmLocation, the name would be pmLocation and the values would be Contra_Near_End_Rx, Contra_Far_End_Rx, Near_End_Rx, Near_End_Tx, Far_End_Rx, Far_End_Tx, Bidirectional.  For thresholdType, the name is thresholdType and the possible values are Low, Lowest, Highest and High.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRelationshipType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRelationshipType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureThresholdRelationship</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdRelationshipType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The kind of relationship between two MetricDefMeasureThresholdRules, such as depends on, follows, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRuleCondition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRuleCondition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdRuleCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A threshold may have two possible values: "Raise" - a threshold was crossed or "Clear" - a threshold ceased crossing.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRuleSeverity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdRuleSeverity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdRuleSeverity</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A threshold can be generated in different severity levels. A crossing for each level may require a different condition and possibly trigger a different consequence.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdTarget -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdTarget">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelObjective</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdTarget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A value that used to specify when a warning should be used that indicates an objective is danger of not being met.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#thresholdType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AnomalyThresholdSet</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>thresholdType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of AnomalyThresholdRule contained in the AnomalyThresholdSet.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ticketType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#ticketType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«JSON::JSON_Attribute»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>ticketType</rdf:label>
