<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>transmissionParameterList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A list of specific parameters related to the layer of the FRE.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#trendIndication -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#trendIndication">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceAlarm</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>trendIndication</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicates the current severity trend of the Managed Object (related to this alarm).  This attribute is not supported in the Simple Alarm Reporting profile and optional in the Standard and Enhanced profiles.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggerConstraints -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggerConstraints">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventTriggerDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>triggerConstraints</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a string that contains the specific OCL expression to constrain how a given set of PolicyEvents are used to trigger the evaluation of the condition clause of a particular PolicyRule. Defining this as an attribute enables external applications to populate the constraint that will be applied to this PolicyRule.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggeringEvent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggeringEvent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SegmentSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>triggeringEvent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The triggeringEvent specifies when the SegmentSpecification has to be evaluated to produce the corresponding Segment. It might be “one shot”, a periodicity or at any update of criteria.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggerPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#triggerPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EventTriggerDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>triggerPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute specifies the start and the of the time period in which this PolicyEvent can be sent to the associated PolicyRule. If the Trigger was not successfully sent (including retries) by this time, then the hasEventEvaluated attribute of each PolicyEvent in this EventSet must be set to 2 (failed to be evaluated).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleDetectionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleDetectionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>troubleDetectionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date on which the trouble was discovered.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>troubleState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The condition of the TroubleTicket as defined by the ITU-X.790 TRState attribute. (deprecated)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleTicketState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#troubleTicketState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TroubleTicket</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>troubleTicketState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The current condition (state) of the TroubleTicket which is a composite of the ITU-X.790 Trouble Ticket state and status attributes. For example, open/active - testing.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#trustLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#trustLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Credential</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>trustLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The trustLevel represents the level of trust of the identification. According to the trustLevel some actions might be available or not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#type -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#type">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>OperationalMarketingPlan</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>type</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type represents the level of OperationalMarketingPlan, i.e. Marketing Plan, Marketing Program or Campaign Plan.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeDependency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeDependency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefMeasureThreshConsDependency</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeDependency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The kind of dependency that exists between the MetricDefMeasureThresholdRule and the MetricDefMeasureConsequence. For example, "the consequence is triggered only if the rule has been applied previously", or "if the rule has already been applied then do not trigger the consequence".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeId -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeId">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>FieldDescriptor</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeId</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TemplateBlock</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfAddress -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfAddress">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddressValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfAddress</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that is used to specify the type of IP address that this instance represents. Values include: 1: IPv4 2: IPv6 3: hostname</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfConnector -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfConnector">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalConnector</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfConnector</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the type of connector that this instance is. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: DB-9  2: DB-15  3: DB-25  4: DB-36  5: DB-60  6: SC  7: SG  to be continued, not done!  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfHolder -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfHolder">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EquipmentHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfHolder</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that identifies the type of the Holder that this object instance is. It is based on M.3100 but includes additional values:  0: Unknown  1: Rack  2: Bay  3: Chassis  4: Shelf  5: Slot  6: Sub-Slot  7: Sub-Rack  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfMemoryComponent -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfMemoryComponent">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MemoryComponent</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfMemoryComponent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the type of memory that this Chip is. Values include: 0: Unknown 1: Proprietary 2: RAM 3: DRAM 4: Synchronous DRAM 5: Cache DRAM 6: EDRAM 7: VRAM 8: SRAM 9: EDO 10: ROM 11: PROM 12: EPROM 13: EEPROM 14: FEPROM 15: Flash 16: CDRAM 17: 3DRAM 18: SDRAM 19: SGRAM 20: RDRAM 21: DDR  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfPower -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfPower">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PowerCapacity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfPower</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer, and defines the type of power that this ManagedHardware unit can accept. Values are:  0: Unknown  1: AC-input  2: DC-input  3: Both AC- and DC-input  Note that a value of 3 means that the Equipment can mix AC- and DC-input power supplies. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfPPort -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfPPort">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalPort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfPPort</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the particular type of PhysicalPort this instance is. Values include:  0: Unknown 1: Ethernet 2: FastEthernet 3: Auto-Sensing 4: GigabitEthernet 5: FastGigabitEthernet 6: DS-0 7: DS-1 8: DS-3 9: T1 10: T3 11: E1 12: E3 13: OC-3 14: OC-12 15: OC-48 16: OC-192 17: RS-232C  This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfRack -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#typeOfRack">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Rack</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>typeOfRack</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the type of Rack. Values include:  0: Unknown  1: Standard 19 Inch  2: Telco  3: Equipment Shelf  4: Non-Standard  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDays -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDays">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unappAppDays</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A day or days representing applicability or un-applicability, for example 2,3 represents Monday and Tuesday. For an instance either unappAppDuration or unappAppDays must have a value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unappAppDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A period of time representing applicability or un-applicability, for example from 8AM to 12PM. For an instance either unappAppDuration or unappAppDays must have a value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDuring -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unappAppDuring">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RevenueAssuranceApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unappAppDuring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A period of time representing applicability or un-applicability. For example, from 8AM to 12PM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unapplicableApplicableCode -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unapplicableApplicableCode">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ServiceLevelSpecApplicability</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unapplicableApplicableCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicator that specifies whether an instance represents applicability or un-applicability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unauthorizedResults -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unauthorizedResults">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityThreatExploit</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unauthorizedResults</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Description the unauthorized results obtained through the use of this exploit</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unique -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unique">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unique</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An indicator that specifies if a value is unique for the specification.  Possible values are; "unique while value is in effect" and "unique whether value is in effect or not"</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#uniquePhysical -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#uniquePhysical">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>HolderAtomic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>uniquePhysical</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute that, if TRUE, means that this holder is physically different from other holders, and is intended to hold a special type of equipment (e.g., a doublewide card, or a longer card than normal). This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#uniqueRequirementsPhysical -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#uniqueRequirementsPhysical">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Card</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>uniqueRequirementsPhysical</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string that contains the physically unique requirements of this Card. For example, it must go in a certain slot number because it has special dimensions. This attribute should only be filled in if the value of the IsUniquePhysical attribute is TRUE; otherwise, it should be NULL.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unit -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unit">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LoyaltyBalance</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unit</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Unit of the quantity credited and debited from the balance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unitCost -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unitCost">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ProjectResourceSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unitCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unitOfMeasure -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#unitOfMeasure">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristicValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>unitOfMeasure</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A length, surface, volume, dry measure, liquid measure, money, weight, time, and the like. Iin general, a determinate quantity or magnitude of the kind designated, taken as a standard of comparison for others of the same kind, in assigning to them numerical values, as 1 foot, 1 yard, 1 mile, 1 square foot.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#upperSize -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#upperSize">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SegmentSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>upperSize</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upperSize specifies the targeted maximum size of the calculated Segment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usage -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usage">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PolicySet</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usage</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string attribute that recommends how this policy object should be used.  Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Usage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date the usage was created.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionDate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionDate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UsageSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageSpecRevisionDate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The date the version was created.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UsageSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageSpecRevisionNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A number that represents the occurrence of the version in the sequence of versions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageSpecRevisionType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>UsageSpecVersion</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageSpecRevisionType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The significance of the revision.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageState -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageState">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Resource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageState</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the current usage of the object. It includes the following values:  0: Unknown  1: Not Installed  2: Installed  3: Inactive  4: Idle  5: Active, but able to communicate  6: Busy (Active and unable to communicate)  Value 2 means that the object is installed (or otherwise activated) but no other information about its state is available. Values 3-6 imply that the object is Installed, and provide further information as to its state.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageStatus -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usageStatus">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Usage</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usageStatus</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The condition of the usage, such as new, processed.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#use -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#use">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntityTypeIdentificationSpec</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>use</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A character that EntityIdentification based on the EntityIdentificationSpec is used as the primary or as a secondary identifier.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usePeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#usePeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RunningSoftwareStatistic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>usePeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The period that the running Software is using a Resource.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#userLabel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#userLabel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CommonObjectInfo</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«likelyToChange»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>userLabel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute represents a provisionable, user friendly name for the object. The userLabel attribute is owned and may be set by the requesting OS or the naming OS.  The difference between the userLabel and the name is that the userLabel is an attribute of the object that may be "set" by the requesting OS or the naming OS.  This attribute may be unique amongst all instances of this object in the target OS.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#userStory -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#userStory">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SCRUM_BacklogItem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>userStory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#UTCOffset -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#UTCOffset">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TimeZoneRule</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>UTCOffset</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4AddressList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4AddressList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv4Variable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v4AddressList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an unordered list of strings, each specifying a single IPv4 address, a hostname, or a range of IPv4 addresses, according to the ABNF definition of an IPv4 address as specified below: IPv4address = 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT IPv4prefix = IPv4address "/" 1*2DIGIT IPv4range = IPv4address"-"IPv4address IPv4maskedaddress = IPv4address","IPv4address Hostnames are defined in RFC1035. In the above definition, each string entry is either: 1. A single Ipv4address in dot notation as defined above. Example: 121.1.1.2 2. A single Hostname. Hostname format follows the guidelines  and restrictions specified in RFC1035. Example: www.bigcompany.com 3. An IPv4range address range defined above, specified by a  start address in dot notation and an end address in dot  notation, separated by "-". The range includes all addresses  between the range's start and end addresses, including the  start and end addresses. Example: 1.1.22.1-1.1.22.5 4. An IPv4maskedaddress address range defined above, specified by an address and mask. The address and mask  are represented in dot notation separated by a comma ",". Example: 2.3.128.0,255.255.248.0. 5. An IPv4prefix address range defined above specified by an  address and a prefix length separated by "/". Example: 2.3.128.0/15</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4Direction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4Direction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv4Variable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v4Direction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines if this variable is used to represent source addresses, destination addresses, or both. Values are: 0: source addresses 1: destination addresses 2: both</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4Format -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4Format">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv4Address</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v4Format</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines the format of the IPv4 address. Values are:  0: dotted decimal  1: CIDR</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4HeaderNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v4HeaderNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv4Variable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v4HeaderNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that defines the particular packet header that contains the IPv4 address information. Specifying the packet header is necessary in case the address is tunneled. In this case, it is mandatory that the correct address be chosen for comparison. Values are: 0: outermost header 1: next innermost header 2: second innermost header etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6AddressList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6AddressList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv6Variable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v6AddressList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an unordered list of strings, each specifying a single IPv6 address, a hostname, or a range of IPv6 addresses, according to the ABNF definition of an IPv6 address as specified below: IPv6address = hexpart [ ":" IPv4address ] IPv4address = 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT "." 1*3DIGIT IPv6prefix = hexpart "/" 1*2DIGIT hexpart = hexseq | hexseq "::" [ hexseq ] | "::" [ hexseq ] hexseq = hex4 *( ":" hex4) hex4 = 1*4HEXDIG IPv6range = IPv6address"-"IPv6address IPv6maskedaddress = IPv6address","IPv6address Hostnames are defined in RFC1035. In the above definition, each string entry is either: 1. A single IPv6address in dot notation as defined above. 2. A single Hostname. Hostname format follows the guidelines  and restrictions specified in RFC1035. 3. An IPv6range address range defined above, specified by a  start address in dot notation and an end address in dot  notation, separated by "-". The range includes all addresses  between the range's start and end addresses, including the  start and end addresses. 4. An IPv6maskedaddress address range defined above, specified by an address and mask. The address and mask  are represented in dot notation separated by a comma ",". 5. An IPv6prefix address range defined above specified by an  address and a prefix length separated by "/".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6Direction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6Direction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv6Variable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v6Direction</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer that defines if this variable is used to represent source addresses, destination addresses, or both.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6HeaderNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#v6HeaderNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPv6FlowIDVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>v6HeaderNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an enumerated integer that defines the particular packet header that contains the IPv6 address information. Specifying the packet header is necessary in case the address is tunneled. In this case, it is mandatory that the correct address be chosen for comparison. Values are: 0: outermost header 1: next innermost header 2: second innermost header etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validFor -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validFor">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>validFor</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The time period that the PartyRole is valid for</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validForManagingResourceRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validForManagingResourceRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ResourceRolePartyRoleDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>validForManagingResourceRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines a starting and ending time period for which it is permissible for this PartyRole to manage this Resource.  TimePeriod is a complex data structure, that consists of a DateStamp and a TimeStamp to define its starting time and ending time.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validityDuration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validityDuration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PartyPrivacyProfileTypeCharValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>validityDuration</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The validityPeriod might be used to specify how long the choice might be valid before going back to the default configuration.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validPeriod -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#validPeriod">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ContactMediumCredentialRole</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>validPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Valid period during which the ContactMedium might be used.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#value -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#value">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristicValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>value</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A discrete value that the characteristic can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueAddressFormat -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueAddressFormat">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IPAddressValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueAddressFormat</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an enumerated integer attribute that contains one of 5 different representations for an address or address range, as specified below: - 0: a single address in dot notation, such as 12.1.1.2 - 1: an address range specified by an address with a prefix, such as 12.1.1.0/15 - 2: an address range specified by a starting address in dot notation and an ending address in dot notation, separated by "-". The range includes all addresses between the range's starting and ending addresses, including these two addresses, such as 12.1.1.3-12.1.22.5 - 3: an address range specified by an address and mask. The address and mask are represented in dot notation, separated by a comma ",", such as 2.3.128.0,255.255.248.0. - 4: a single Hostname, as specified in RFC1035</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueBitStringList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueBitStringList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BitStringValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueBitStringList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an array of strings, defined in an unordered list , each representing a single bit string or a set of bit strings. Each string entry is either: - a single bit string, such as 11110101 - a range of bit strings specified using a bit string and a bit mask. The bit string and mask fields must have the same  number of bits specified. The mask bit string specifies the  significant bits in the bit string value. An example is: 100110,101110</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueBooleanList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueBooleanList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BooleanValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueBooleanList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a Boolean attribute, whose value is used to represent a Boolean policy value.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueConstraint -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueConstraint">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ValueConstraintDetails</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueConstraint</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is a string that contains the specific OCL expression to define how a given PolicyValue is constrained by a particular PolicyVariable. Defining this as an attribute enables external applications to populate this constraint.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueFrom -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueFrom">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CharacteristicSpecValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueFrom</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The low range value that a characteristic can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueIntegerList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueIntegerList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>IntegerValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueIntegerList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an array of strings, defined as an unordered list, where each integer in the list is represented by a string. This is done to accommodate the reserved words "INFINITY" and "-INFINITY". The format of this attribute takes one of the following two forms: - a single integer value - a range of integers. The range is specified by a starting integer and an ending integer, separated by '..'. The starting integer must be less than or equal to the ending integer. The range includes all integers between the  starting and ending integers, including these two integers. To represent a range of integers that is not bounded, the reserved words "-INFINITY" and/or "INFINITY" can be used in place of the starting and ending integers.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueModelAttribute -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueModelAttribute">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ValueCustom</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueModelAttribute</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the name of the attribute within the class specified in the valueModelClass attribute that is to be evaluated or set as a PolicyValue. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueModelClass -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueModelClass">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ValueCustom</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueModelClass</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the class name whose attribute is to be evaluated or set as a PolicyValue. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueStringList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueStringList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StringValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueStringList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an array of strings, defined in an unordered list, each representing a single string. Any string can have one or more wildcards, denoted with the asterisk character (*). For example, the value "abc*def*" matches the string "abcxxxdefyz". If the asterisk character is required as part of the string value itself, it must be escaped with quotes (").</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueTo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueTo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>CharacteristicSpecValue</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueTo</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The upper range value that a characteristic can take on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#valueType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MarketSegmentCharacteristic</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>valueType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A kind of value that the characteristic can take on, such as numeric, text, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableBitStringList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableBitStringList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>BitStringVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>variableBitStringList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an unordered list of strings, each representing  a single bit string or a set of bit strings. The number of bits  specified SHOULD equal the number of bits of the expected variable. For example, for an 8-bit byte variable, 8 bits should be specified. If the variable does not have a fixed length, the most significant bits should be used. The formal definition of a bit string is: binary-digit = "0" / "1" bitstring = 1*binary-digit maskedBitString = bitstring","bitstring Each string entry is either: 1. A single bit string. Example: 00111010 2. A range of bit strings specifies using a bit string and a bit mask. The bit string and mask properties have the same  number of bits specified. The mask bit string specifies the  significant bits in the bit string value. For example, 110110,  100110 and 110111 would match the maskedBitString  100110,101110 but 100100 would not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableDNList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableDNList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>DNVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>variableDNList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute provides an unordered list of strings, each representing a Distinguished Name (DN) with wildcards. The asterisk character ("*") is used as wildcard for either a single attribute value or a wildcard for an RDN.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableModelAttribute -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableModelAttribute">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VariableCustom</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>variableModelAttribute</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the name of the attribute within the class specified in the variableModelClass attribute that is to be evaluated or set as a PolicyVariable. This enables the VariableCustom class to point to other attributes of other classes that can be defined as extensions of the standard model. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs. The IETF RFCs only define “MATCH”.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableModelClass -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableModelClass">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>VariableCustom</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>variableModelClass</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string attribute that defines the class name whose attribute is to be evaluated or set as a PolicyVariable. This enables the VariableCustom class to point to other attributes of other classes that can be defined as extensions of the standard  model. Notes: Not present in the ITU or CIM specs. The IETF RFCs only define “MATCH”.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableStringList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#variableStringList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>StringVariable</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>variableStringList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute is an unordered list of strings, each representing  a single string with wildcards. The asterisk character "*" is used as a wildcard, and represents an arbitrary sub-string replacement. For example, the value "abc*def" match "abcxyzdef", and the value "abc*def*" match "abcxxxdefyyyzzz".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vendorName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vendorName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResourceSpecAttributes</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>vendorName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that defines the name of the manufacturer. This, in combination with the ModelNumber and the PartNumber, identify different types of hardware items. The SerialNumber can then be used to differentiate between different instances of the same type of hardware item. This is a REQUIRED attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vendorPortName -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vendorPortName">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalPort</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>vendorPortName</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that contains the vendor-specific name of this port. This is different from the commonName attribute, which represents a system-wide naming structure for all ManagedEntities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#version -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#version">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ConfigurationSpecification</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>version</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A particular form of a ConfigurationSpecification that differs in certain respects from an earlier ConfigurationSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#versionNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#versionNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Project</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>versionNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Allows us to keep track of updates to the Project</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#versionNumber -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#versionNumber">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>PhysicalResource</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>versionNumber</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a string that identifies the version of this object. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#visibleAlarm -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#visibleAlarm">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>visibleAlarm</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a boolean attribute that, if TRUE, indicates that the SecureHolder is equipped with one or more visible alarms (e.g., LEDs or gauges). This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#visibleAlarmDescription -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#visibleAlarmDescription">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecureHolder</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>visibleAlarmDescription</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a free-form string attribute that provides supplementary information for the VisibleAlarm attribute. It should only be filled in when the value of VisibleAlarm is TRUE.  This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vlanIdRange -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vlanIdRange">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>TrafficMappingTableRow</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>vlanIdRange</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute states the VLAN ID or VLAN ID range to which the row applies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vulnerabilityScore -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#vulnerabilityScore">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityVulnerabilityScore</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>vulnerabilityScore</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The value of the SecurityVulnerabilityScore calculated using a SecurityVulnerabilityScoringAlgorithm.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wasRoutedByNetwork -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wasRoutedByNetwork">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>ForwardingRelationshipEncapsulation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>wasRoutedByNetwork</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute indicates if the current route of the FRE was computed by the managed system (i.e. "the network", all capabilities below the interface that defines the perspectiveof managed system) or not (e.g. the route was provided over an interface by a client EMS).   If rerouting is allowed, this attribute identifies whether the routing was carried out by "the network" or not.  If there is no network routing capability the attribute should be set to False.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wbsLevel -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wbsLevel">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WBSElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>wbsLevel</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The level that this WBS is in the Project's WBS hierarchy</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wbsNr -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#wbsNr">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>WBSElement</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>wbsNr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A unique identifier for the WBS, usually defined as a structured set of numbers e.g. 1003.8842.36 may identify a level 3 WBS withing a Project.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weaknessAllowingIncidentToOccur -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weaknessAllowingIncidentToOccur">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>SecurityIncidentAssessment</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>weaknessAllowingIncidentToOccur</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Weakness that allowed the incident to take place. Enumerated List:  No AntiVirus Signature AntiVirus Not Turned On AntiVirus Not Up To Date AntiVirus Not Properly Configured AntiVirus Software Not Installed No Patch Available Not Patched Patch Installed but Not Effective Currently Under Extension (Waiver Status) Weak Password Poor System Configuration Poor Network Configuration Social Engineering Inside No Policy Available Policy Enforced Compromised Information Trusted Network Access Other</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weight -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weight">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>weight</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the weight of the ManagedComponent using the units specified in the WeightUnits attribute. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weightUnits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#weightUnits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>weightUnits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the Units for the Weight attribute of this object. Values include:  0: Unknown (Not Measured)  1: ounces  2: pounds  3: grams  4: kilograms  This is an optional attribute. However, if Weight attribute is defined, then this attribute is REQUIRED.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#width -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#width">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>Hardware</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>width</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This attribute defines the width of the ManagedComponent using the units specified in the MeasurementUnits attribute. This is an optional attribute.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#workflowType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#workflowType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>EntitySpecificationActionWorkflow</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>workflowType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The type of this workflow instance like script, fulfilment plan and so on.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#writingProficiency -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#writingProficiency">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LanguageAbility</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>writingProficiency</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Degree of mastery in writing a language.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#x -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#x">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>x</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The x Cartesian coordinate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#xLSFormula -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#xLSFormula">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>MetricDefinitionDeterminationMethod</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>xLSFormula</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A precise XLS-compatible formula using XLS named ranges (from XLS Name field).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#xUnits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#xUnits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalCoordinateSystem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>xUnits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The unit for a number in the X direction in a local location. Notes: units could be metres, feet, inches …</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#y -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#y">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>«required»</TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>y</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The y Cartesian coordinate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#yUnits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#yUnits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalCoordinateSystem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>yUnits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The unit for a number in the Y direction in a local location. Notes: units could be metres, feet, inches …</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#z -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#z">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>AbsoluteLocalLocation</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>z</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The z Cartesian coordinate. Note: required for 3D representations</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#zUnits -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#zUnits">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/><TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>LocalCoordinateSystem</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype><rdf:label>zUnits</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The unit for a number in the Z direction in a local location. Notes: units could be metres, feet, inches …</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

